ttps://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gkrajniak","id":7794387,"login":"gkrajniak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTQzODc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/portal-ui-lib/commits/d5b14e655944d723807dd2f02deb5e25ef620a09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T08:52:07Z","email":"gkrajniak@gmail.com","name":"Grzegorz Krajniak"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T08:52:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/angular 22 support (#696)\n\nfeat: add Angular 22 support\nAdds Angular 22 to the supported range for @openmfp/portal-ui-lib while\nkeeping backward compatibility with Angular 20 and 21. Luigi and\nFundamental-ngx already ship Angular-22-compatible releases\n(@luigi-project/client-support-angular@22,\n@fundamental-ngx/ui5-webcomponents\n@0.64), so the ecosystem is ready.\n\npeerDependencies (widened, back-compat preserved):\n- @angular/* -> ^20.3.14 || ^21.1.2 || ^21.2.0 || ^22.0.0 (restored\n  @angular/compiler + @angular/elements that ng update had dropped)\n- @fundamental-ngx/ui5-webcomponents -> ... || ^0.64.0\n- @luigi-project/client-support-angular -> ... || ^22.0.0\n- apollo-angular -> ^13.0.0 || ^14.1.0\n\ndevDependencies (build/verify against Angular 22, via `ng update`):\n- @angular/* + @angular/cli + @angular-devkit/build-angular -> 22.1.x,\n  ng-packagr 22.1.1, typescript 6.0.3, @angular/cdk 22.1.2\n- @angular-eslint/* -> 22.1.0 (required by @angular/cli@22); overrides\npin\n  angular-eslint@^22 for @openmfp/eslint-config-typescript, which still\n  peer-caps at 21\n- @fundamental-ngx/ui5-webcomponents (dev) -> 0.64.1\n- add @types/lodash.isequal, @types/lodash.ismatch\n\nCode: Angular 22 / TypeScript 6 enable stricter type-checking. Annotated\nimplicit-any Luigi callback params, typed string-indexed maps as\nRecord<>,\nadded definite-assignment (!) to lazy caches, narrowed caught `unknown`\nerrors, and added an ambient module decl for\n@luigi-project/plugin-auth-oauth2\n(no published https://github.com/types). Applied across source and spec\nfiles.\n\nESLint: migrated the legacy `.eslintrc.json` to flat config\n(`eslint.config.mjs`) because https://github.com/angular-eslint@22 is\nflat-config-only. Ports\nthe `lib` selector prefixes, enables type-aware linting, and pins the\njest\nplugin version (repo uses vitest). Pre-existing lint findings (mostly\nno-explicit-any) that the old config never enforced are left as separate\nlint-debt cleanup.\n\nVerified: `npm run build` (lib + wc) and `npm test` (469 tests) pass on\nAngular 22; `ng lint` runs under the new flat config.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added support for Angular 22 and updated related development tooling.\n* Improved TypeScript type coverage and compatibility for public APIs\nand configuration helpers.\n  * Added ambient type support for the OAuth authentication plugin.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Improved initialization error logging to handle different error\nformats safely.\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Refreshed setup, configuration, contribution, and feature\ndocumentation with clearer examples and formatting.\n\n* **Chores**\n* Replaced the previous lint configuration with the current ESLint\nsetup.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"4d49af67e37eb52e4722e3709e3cef166ed4f9a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/portal-ui-lib/git/trees/4d49af67e37eb52e4722e3709e3cef166ed4f9a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/portal-ui-lib/git/commits/d5b14e655944d723807dd2f02deb5e25ef620a09","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d49af67e37eb52e4722e3709e3cef166ed4f9a4\nparent 77c0452157d6983b8eb7695f5402f1c1afb65206\nauthor Grzegorz Krajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com> 1786697527 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786697527 +0200\n\nFeat/angular 22 support (#696)\n\nfeat: add Angular 22 support\nAdds Angular 22 to the supported range for @openmfp/portal-ui-lib while\nkeeping backward compatibility with Angular 20 and 21. Luigi and\nFundamental-ngx already ship Angular-22-compatible releases\n(@luigi-project/client-support-angular@22,\n@fundamental-ngx/ui5-webcomponents\n@0.64), so the ecosystem is ready.\n\npeerDependencies (widened, back-compat preserved):\n- @angular/* -> ^20.3.14 || ^21.1.2 || ^21.2.0 || ^22.0.0 (restored\n  @angular/compiler + @angular/elements that ng update had dropped)\n- @fundamental-ngx/ui5-webcomponents -> ... || ^0.64.0\n- @luigi-project/client-support-angular -> ... || ^22.0.0\n- apollo-angular -> ^13.0.0 || ^14.1.0\n\ndevDependencies (build/verify against Angular 22, via `ng update`):\n- @angular/* + @angular/cli + @angular-devkit/build-angular -> 22.1.x,\n  ng-packagr 22.1.1, typescript 6.0.3, @angular/cdk 22.1.2\n- @angular-eslint/* -> 22.1.0 (required by @angular/cli@22); overrides\npin\n  angular-eslint@^22 for @openmfp/eslint-config-typescript, which still\n  peer-caps at 21\n- @fundamental-ngx/ui5-webcomponents (dev) -> 0.64.1\n- add @types/lodash.isequal, @types/lodash.ismatch\n\nCode: Angular 22 / TypeScript 6 enable stricter type-checking. Annotated\nimplicit-any Luigi callback params, typed string-indexed maps as\nRecord<>,\nadded definite-assignment (!) to lazy caches, narrowed caught `unknown`\nerrors, and added an ambient module decl for\n@luigi-project/plugin-auth-oauth2\n(no published https://github.com/types). Applied across source and spec\nfiles.\n\nESLint: migrated the legacy `.eslintrc.json` to flat config\n(`eslint.config.mjs`) because https://github.com/angular-eslint@22 is\nflat-config-only. Ports\nthe `lib` selector prefixes, enables type-aware linting, and pins the\njest\nplugin version (repo uses vitest). Pre-existing lint findings (mostly\nno-explicit-any) that the old config never enforced are left as separate\nlint-debt cleanup.\n\nVerified: `npm run build` (lib + wc) and `npm test` (469 tests) pass on\nAngular 22; `ng lint` runs under the new flat config.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added support for Angular 22 and updated related development tooling.\n* Improved TypeScript type coverage and compatibility for public APIs\nand configuration helpers.\n  * Added ambient type support for the OAuth authentication plugin.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Improved initialization error logging to handle different error\nformats safely.\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Refreshed setup, configuration, contribution, and feature\ndocumentation with clearer examples and formatting.\n\n* **Chores**\n* Replaced the previous lint configuration with the current ESLint\nsetup.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqftc3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2C4QAIiylr+EXCTWp03xBUP8VidD\nAtnKDdYiMUyriptPmy4UGuxMV+pX9EOYCAf/fwhXiaLGAgN+1Ss0HAXwmiBzwixg\nMa248Iq/qz7M1dlymzSOD1vsTSoidyXeIpxecrH3UosaUBu9Xlln/Ca/q37zU1fW\nxg+ciTR7Py6UHbUXx1CRXo60xatVS6nRlY3Nb5GhPPS/edxaVwvSGiK4KV8aHB4A\n24gLaxIaNUzLxg+SBffr5FeIIL2qmnT8H04FD4061+5qNLU9XiBoMFs8gbaqsJEq\nIkGMvY82UTX2B9du