_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/15e6c834437ed5932cc96e346e5b06fee3ab0611/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:39:06Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:39:06Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Make the Windows and pnpm jobs actually run\n\nTwo ways of spawning npm are wrong on Windows, and the first fix picked the\nother one. `execFileSync(''npm'', …)` fails with ENOENT because npm is `npm.cmd`\nthere; `execFileSync(''npm.cmd'', …)` fails with EINVAL because Node refuses to\nspawn a `.cmd` without a shell, which is the fix for the Windows\nargument-injection CVE. Both tests now go through npm''s own JS entry point —\n`npm_execpath`, which npm sets when it runs a script — with the current Node\nbinary, so it is a plain executable spawn everywhere and no shell is involved.\nOne of the two call sites had also been missed entirely, because prettier had\nwrapped it across lines and the edit matched the single-line form.\n\nThe pnpm job needed a different shape, not a different command. `pnpm add\n<tarball>` resolves the WHOLE manifest before it applies its argument, and a\ngenerated project pins the SDK exactly during the preview — a version that is\nnot on the registry until this candidate is published. So `add` fails before it\ncan help, in every form, and so does any second argument-less install. Pointing\nthe manifest at the tarball first and then running a plain install is the one\nshape both managers accept; it also leaves package.json saying which file went\nin. Verified locally end to end under both, including that pnpm resolves the\nruntime plugin from inside the installed package.\n\nThe ledger digest test passed on Windows this time, so the .gitattributes fix\nholds: what remained was the tarball test failing because npm could not be\nspawned at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9b93f551887da9aee48f64e49ee6fa477bdcc72d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/9b93f551887da9aee48f64e49ee6fa477bdcc72d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/15e6c834437ed5932cc96e346e5b06fee3ab0611","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/15e6c834437ed5932cc96e346e5b06fee3ab0611","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDE1ZTZjODM0NDM3ZWQ1OTMyY2M5NmUzNDZlNWIwNmZlZTNhYjA2MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/648b1dbe354c0001b73cdc178f30613fbc1553ec","sha":"648b1dbe354c0001b73cdc178f30613fbc1553ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/648b1dbe354c0001b73cdc178f30613fbc1553ec"}],"sha":"15e6c834437ed5932cc96e346e5b06fee3ab0611","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/15e6c834437ed5932cc96e346e5b06fee3ab0611"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/648b1dbe354c0001b73cdc178f30613fbc1553ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:26:17Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:26:33Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Fix what the second review round and CI found, including two half-fixes\n\nThe previous round''s fixes were incomplete in a way worth naming: I fixed the\ncases that were reported rather than the class they belonged to. `exposes`,\n`shared` and `remotes` were guarded against non-array values while\n`configuredShared` and `configuredRemote` — checked with `=== undefined`, which\nlets `null` through — kept throwing. The recursive scan learned to skip\nnon-regular files while the two DIRECT reads above it did not, so a FIFO named\nremoteEntry.js still hangs `cyweb-app verify` forever. Both are fixed, and the\ncontract is now asserted over eighteen shapes a corrupt manifest can take,\nrather than over the shapes someone happened to report.\n\n`ABSOLUTE_NODE_MODULES` carried the `g` flag and was used with `.test()`, which\nkeeps `lastIndex` between calls: three chunks that all carry an absolute\nbuild-machine path came back as the first and the third. The check that those\npaths stay confined to remoteEntry.js was passing while chunks carried them.\nCounting and testing now use separate regexes, and a fixture with three leaking\nchunks proves all three are named.\n\n`buildStart` removed a path built from an unbounded id and version, so a\n300-character prerelease — legal SemVer, accepted by the runtime reader — failed\nwith ENAMETOOLONG instead of the submission-profile violation that is the actual\nproblem, and the reason the profile bounds the version at all.\n\nThe readiness warning said a field \"is not declared in package.json\" when\nnormalization had DROPPED a declared one, contradicting the specific warning\nprinted immediately above it.\n\nCI was failing on all of this and on three more. `pnpm install` takes no package\nargument — that is `pnpm add` — and with `--silent` it fails with no output at\nall, which is how the pnpm job came to end right after the scaffolder''s banner\nwith a bare exit 1. On Windows `npm` is `npm.cmd`, which `execFileSync` cannot\nlaunch. And MSYS `mkfifo` succeeds without creating a FIFO, so the tests now\ncheck `isFIFO()` and skip rather than assert against a shim.\n\nThe ledger digest mismatch was the most interesting: CI computed `c4ac157f…`\nfor a schema recorded as `67777152…`, which is exactly the CRLF hash of the same\nbytes. The design says digests are taken over raw bytes with no newline\nnormalization — and Git normalizes newlines on a Windows checkout unless told\nnot to. A digest that depends on who checked the repository out pins nothing, so\n`schema/**` is `-text`, the tree is `eol=lf`, and §3.2 now records why.\n\nBoth bots also flagged `${{ inputs.tag }}` interpolated into release `run`\nblocks: GitHub expands it before the shell parses, so shell syntax in a\nfree-form workflow input executes in the release job. It now reaches the shell\nthrough the environment, in all four steps.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e286fc8efec1037f9416ae939d79b2efdd51e75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/1e286fc8efec1037f9416ae939d79b2efdd51e75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/648b1dbe354c0001b73cdc178f30613fbc1553ec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/648b1dbe354c0001b73cdc178f30613fbc1553ec","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDY0OGIxZGJlMzU0YzAwMDFiNzNjZGMxNzhmMzA2MTNmYmMxNTUzZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/241b6421080f850afe3c78e31e9073653c8d9ce1","sha":"241b6421080f850afe3c78e31e9073653c8d9ce1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/241b6421080f850afe3c78e31e9073653c8d9ce1"}],"sha":"648b1dbe354c0001b73cdc178f30613fbc1553ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/648b1dbe354c0001b73cdc178f30613fbc1553ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/241b6421080f850afe3c78e31e9073653c8d9ce1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T03:56:36Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T03:56:36Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Fix nine defects the PR review found, and the invariant that hid three of them\n\nThree of these were the same class of defect wearing different clothes: the\nproducer could emit a manifest its OWN wire validator rejects. An SSH URL''s\npassword was dropped rather than refused, so a credential committed to\npackage.json would have reached a public manifest as if it had never been\nthere. `…/repo.git/` kept its suffix, because `.git$` does not match a path\nending in a slash. A homepage inside its limit going in came out over it,\nbecause the URL parser percent-encodes a non-ASCII path. Each is fixed, and\n`buildCyManifest` now runs the wire validator over what it built and treats a\nfailure as an SDK bug rather than the developer''s — the assertion the design\nmade three times and checked zero.\n\nTwo more were reads that never returned. A FIFO named `assets/pipe.js` hung the\nverifier forever, because it reads every .js file and `readFileSync` on a FIFO\nblocks until a writer appears; the earlier FIFO test used an extensionless name\nand so never touched it. The packager now walks and validates file types BEFORE\nverification, and the verifier collects regular files only. And\n`{ \"exposes\": {} }` threw a TypeError out of a function whose contract is to\nreturn failures — `typeof x === \"object\"` was never enough for that promise,\nand the packager calls the core without the CLI wrapper''s catch, so it surfaced\nas a build crash naming nothing.\n\nThe rest are narrower. The scaffolder split versions on every hyphen, so\n`1.0.0-alpha-9007199254740992` warned about a numeric identifier that is\nactually part of one alphanumeric one — the scaffolder and the packager\ndisagreeing about a rule they are supposed to share. `--out=a --out=b` slipped\npast the duplicate check, which compared whole tokens, while two identical\n`--expect-expose=./A` tokens were wrongly rejected as duplicates of a repeatable\nflag. The registry read-back ran under `set -uo pipefail` without `-e`, so a\nfailed tag assertion on the first package left the step green if the second\nsucceeded — in the one check that exists to catch a mis-tagged release. And a\npackage.json comment claimed the corpora are digest-pinned; they are shipped\nconformance examples, carry no `$id`, and are not in the ledger.\n\nOne finding is declined. Issue #8 asks for \"a single entry for the generated\napplication (rather than a list)\", modelled on apps.json — which is what this\nis. The review read it as requiring apps.json''s array shape.\n\nReordering the walk ahead of verification changed one message for the better: a\nbroken symlink is now rejected by name instead of arriving as an ENOENT from a\nfile read, which named the symptom rather than the cause.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4c08a77da36e4f38984f794770509ca9f853c9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/d4c08a77da36e4f38984f794770509ca9f853c9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/241b6421080f850afe3c78e31e9073653c8d9ce1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/241b6421080f850afe3c78e31e9073653c8d9ce1","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDI0MWI2NDIxMDgwZjg1MGFmZTNjNzhlMzFlOTA3MzY1M2M4ZDljZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/76f046e9b440d65ca19e5917754970743e447a98","sha":"76f046e9b440d65ca19e5917754970743e447a98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/76f046e9b440d65ca19e5917754970743e447a98"}],"sha":"241b6421080f850afe3c78e31e9073653c8d9ce1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/241b6421080f850afe3c78e31e9073653c8d9ce1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/76f046e9b440d65ca19e5917754970743e447a98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T23:24:50Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T23:24:50Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"0.4.0-next.1: the submission manifest, as a Developer Preview\n\nBoth packages move to 0.4.0-next.1 in lockstep, and so does everything that\nnames them. The five examples had to move too: `^0.3.0` does not admit a\nprerelease, so npm would have gone looking for 0.4.0-next.1 on a registry that\ndoes not have it yet rather than linking the workspace copy.\n\nGenerated projects pin the preview EXACTLY. A caret over a prerelease admits\nonly prereleases of the same major.minor.patch — neither the stability an exact\npin gives nor the breadth a caret suggests — and the SDK_VERSION test picks\nwhich rule applies from whether the runtime''s own version is a prerelease, so\nthe pin and the runtime cannot drift apart in either direction.\n\nThe schema and predicate identities stay under /draft/, and no document claims\nformatVersion 1 is stable. Issuing the stable identity freezes the envelope, and\nthat waits on the handshake in issue #8.\n\nOne test was depending on suite order. The byte-identity check between the CLI\nand the packager read whichever archive happened to be lying around, so it\nstarted failing the moment the version bumped: a stale archive carries the\ngenerator string of whatever SDK built it. It now builds its own archive from a\nfixture both suites share.\n\nPrepared, not published. Publishing runs from the release workflow after this\nmerges, so the artifact and its provenance attest to a commit on the main line\nrather than to a feature branch. Rehearsed locally: 49 files, 65.8 kB, the\ntemplates present in the scaffolder tarball, and the repository field the\nregistry validates and a dry run never sees.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"919601cbcb589dc84adbf6cce67044a4979aa497","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/919601cbcb589dc84adbf6cce67044a4979aa497"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/76f046e9b440d65ca19e5917754970743e447a98","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/76f046e9b440d65ca19e5917754970743e447a98","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDc2ZjA0NmU5YjQ0MGQ2NWNhMTllNTkxNzc1NDk3MDc0M2U0NDdhOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4c68dbd122df48fd23561fa5c785f2f7f93c807e","sha":"4c68dbd122df48fd23561fa5c785f2f7f93c807e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4c68dbd122df48fd23561fa5c785f2f7f93c807e"}],"sha":"76f046e9b440d65ca19e5917754970743e447a98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/76f046e9b440d65ca19e5917754970743e447a98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4c68dbd122df48fd23561fa5c785f2f7f93c807e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:44:05Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:44:05Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Ship the manifest to generated projects, the examples, and CI\n\nEverything the packager can do was only reachable from this monorepo, where\nadm-zip arrives transitively through the Federation plugin and `build:zip`\ntherefore works by accident. Generated projects now declare it themselves,\nbecause a project relying on that would break the day that plugin stopped\nneeding it. The five maintained examples gain the script and both of its\ndependencies — none of them declared `cross-env` either, and the repository root\ndoes not provide it, so adding only the script would have shipped a documented\ncommand that does not run. All five now build an archive: 18, 10, 18, 16 and 14\nmembers, each with one root manifest and one root entry and no HTML, source map\nor Federation metadata.\n\nThe scaffolder gained the half of the version rule that is not a refusal. A\nversion outside the submission profile — build metadata, over-length, a numeric\nidentifier past MAX_SAFE_INTEGER — is legal SemVer and builds and runs fine; the\nrule is about a ZIP filename and a URL path segment. So it warns on stderr,\nexits 0, and writes the project, and `build:zip` is where it actually fails. All\nthree halves are verified end to end. `cy-manifest.json` joins the generated\n.gitignore, since a copy committed beside the package.json it is derived from is\na second source of truth nothing keeps in step.\n\nCI stops testing the wrong thing. The scaffold job installed the REGISTRY copy\nof app-runtime whenever the generated range already resolved, using the\ncandidate tarball only as a fallback — so an ordinary SDK change could pass a\npre-publish gate while exercising code published weeks ago. It now always\ninstalls the candidate, asserts the resolved package sits inside the generated\nproject, and asserts `cyweb-app --version` matches it. It runs under npm AND\npnpm, which the SDK design already made an acceptance criterion but which only\nnpm had ever satisfied, and under pnpm it asserts the runtime plugin resolves\ninside the installed package — a path escaping it fails silently at load time.\nEach template now also builds an archive and reads the manifest back out.\n\nA windows-latest job covers what no amount of Linux testing reveals: rename over\nan existing file, separators in member names, and the order they come out in.\nThe packager turns adm-zip''s locale-dependent sorting off and uses one named\ncomparator precisely so the answer is the same on both, which is only worth\nclaiming if it is executed somewhere.\n\nPost-publish smoke follows the workflow''s `tag` input rather than a hard-coded\n`next` — the workflow can publish `latest` — asserts the tag actually moved\ninstead of printing it beside the version, then installs through the tag,\nscaffolds, and reads a manifest out of a real archive.\n\nDocs: getting-started §5b said `npm run build` writes the zip, which stopped\nbeing true when the zip became opt-in and stayed on the page for longer than it\nshould have.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f02f00011b6f31d4a1ec4a9dba9e36ce02576f08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/f02f00011b6f31d4a1ec4a9dba9e36ce02576f08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/4c68dbd122df48fd23561fa5c785f2f7f93c807e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4c68dbd122df48fd23561fa5c785f2f7f93c807e","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDRjNjhkYmQxMjJkZjQ4ZmQyMzU2MWZhNWM3ODVmMmY3ZjkzYzgwN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/797893d0c77f8537f07a546b0b95503551800746","sha":"797893d0c77f8537f07a546b0b95503551800746","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/797893d0c77f8537f07a546b0b95503551800746"}],"sha":"4c68dbd122df48fd23561fa5c785f2f7f93c807e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4c68dbd122df48fd23561fa5c785f2f7f93c807e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/797893d0c77f8537f07a546b0b95503551800746/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:27:00Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:27:00Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Add `cyweb-app manifest`, and give the CLI a grammar worth testing\n\nThe App Store''s build-from-GitHub path never runs a zip build, so without a\nnon-archive entry point it could not obtain a manifest at all. `manifest` shares\nthe builder with the packager and, more to the point, the SERIALIZER: the copy\nthis prints and the copy embedded in an archive are 429 bytes either way for\nhello-world, compared with Buffer.compare. Sharing a builder would have made\nthem equal objects; sharing a serializer makes them equal files.\n\nstdout carries JSON and nothing else — readiness warnings and diagnostics go to\nstderr, and stdout is empty when --out is used — so `cyweb-app manifest > file`\nis a usable thing to type. Exit codes are stated and tested: 2 for a usage\nerror, 1 for work that failed, 0 for success.\n\nThe grammar moved into its own module so the matrix can run without spawning a\nprocess per case, and it enforces two rules `parseArgs` does not. A singleton\nflag given twice is an error rather than a silent last-one-wins, because\n`--out a.json --out b.json` would otherwise write one and say nothing about the\nother. And a flag-shaped value given with `=` is an error: parseArgs calls\n`--root --out x` ambiguous on its own, but accepts `--root=--out` without\ncomplaint, and the developer then gets \"cannot read package.json\" instead of a\nusage error. `-h` and `-v` are kept — they are existing public behaviour, and\ndropping them would break anyone who has typed them into a script.\n\n`--out` is deliberately unrestricted: it is a path the developer types, not one\nderived from untrusted metadata, so it is treated like a shell redirect with\n--force as the explicit overwrite. What revision 3 called protection — refusing\ntwo specific basenames — is gone, because partial protection described as\ncontainment is worse than none. What replaces it are the surprises rather than\nthe permissions: an existing file is not overwritten silently, a symlink or a\nsymlinked ancestor is not written THROUGH, a missing parent directory is\nreported rather than created, and the write goes through a temp file beside the\ndestination because a rename across filesystems fails with EXDEV.\n\nThe process-level cases run against a freshly packed candidate rather than the\nworkspace dist/, and assert they are running the extracted binary — a stale\nbuild passing its own tests is the failure that makes a CLI suite worthless.\nThe Windows leg of the matrix is named as Phase 6''s CI rather than claimed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f7597d4c8dd09cf50aeb5c7941541599a6be062d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/f7597d4c8dd09cf50aeb5c7941541599a6be062d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/797893d0c77f8537f07a546b0b95503551800746","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/797893d0c77f8537f07a546b0b95503551800746","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDc5Nzg5M2QwYzc3Zjg1MzdmMDdhNTQ2YjBiOTU1MDM1NTE4MDA3NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/52093b9fe29efc6382f5c7ef24ba26f96f1adc5b","sha":"52093b9fe29efc6382f5c7ef24ba26f96f1adc5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/52093b9fe29efc6382f5c7ef24ba26f96f1adc5b"}],"sha":"797893d0c77f8537f07a546b0b95503551800746","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/797893d0c77f8537f07a546b0b95503551800746"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/52093b9fe29efc6382f5c7ef24ba26f96f1adc5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:09:47Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:09:47Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Package the archive: verify first, deny before allow, rename last\n\nThe packager now writes the submission manifest into the archive, and everything\naround that write exists for a failure that has happened.\n\nIt verifies before it packages, with the snapshot defineCyWebApp already took,\nso a build that does not satisfy the federation contract is never uploaded and\nthe identity checked is the identity written. It escalates the verifier''s note\nabout absolute build-machine paths into a warning, because that note is about\nexactly this case: a developer ZIP, not a CI runner.\n\nClassification is denies before allows, and the deny classes are named. An\nextension allowlist alone readmits what must not ship — mf-manifest.json and\nmf-stats.json are .json, the SSR chunks are .js — and the SSR chunks carry\ncontent hashes, so they are denied by prefix rather than by name. HTML and\nsource maps are denied by suffix, which is what catches assets/nested/page.html\nand assets/chunk.js.map. Every deny is tested beside an allowed near-neighbour,\nso a later refactor cannot widen a prefix unnoticed.\n\nTwo things the archive format needed turned out to be someone else''s decision\nuntil now. adm-zip sorts entries by `entryName.toLowerCase().localeCompare(...)`,\nwhich depends on the host''s ICU data — so the same build could produce\ndifferently ordered archives on two machines. Its sorting is off, and a named\ncomparator over unsigned UTF-8 bytes decides. And members are added by name\nrather than by local path, because addLocalFile derives the member name from the\nhost filesystem''s separator.\n\nThe walk rejects symlinks and anything that is not a regular file: addLocalFile\nwould otherwise have stored a link target''s CONTENT as an ordinary member,\nleaving the Store unable to tell a regular-looking file came from outside the\nbuild. A dangling link turned out to reach the verifier first, where it threw\nENOENT out of a file read — a corrupt build output is a result, not an\nexception, so unreadable files are now reported once each and the remaining\nchecks still run.\n\nThe stale-output guarantee is scoped to what it can actually promise: nothing\nstale or partial at the path THIS run computed, after a failure following\nbuildStart. An earlier version''s archive stays, and a fixture proves it —\nremoving files this run cannot name is how a packager deletes a release someone\nstill wanted. The write goes through a temp file beside the destination, never\nan OS temp directory, because a rename across filesystems fails with EXDEV.\n\nzipForAppStore is no longer exported from ./vite. A direct caller would bypass\nthe reader and validation lifecycle the snapshot split exists to enforce; it now\ntakes that snapshot''s two halves and this SDK''s own version, and a test proves a\npackage.json edited mid-build changes neither the archive name nor its contents.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cfc95f645f8063316528ee229c4358690b0b54dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/cfc95f645f8063316528ee229c4358690b0b54dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/52093b9fe29efc6382f5c7ef24ba26f96f1adc5b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/52093b9fe29efc6382f5c7ef24ba26f96f1adc5b","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDUyMDkzYjlmZTI5ZWZjNjM4MmY1YzdlZjI0YmEyNmY5NmYxYWRjNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/8620fe4cb126d86e53cc4ef2c48e746b84e3cd94","sha":"8620fe4cb126d86e53cc4ef2c48e746b84e3cd94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/8620fe4cb126d86e53cc4ef2c48e746b84e3cd94"}],"sha":"52093b9fe29efc6382f5c7ef24ba26f96f1adc5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/52093b9fe29efc6382f5c7ef24ba26f96f1adc5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/8620fe4cb126d86e53cc4ef2c48e746b84e3cd94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T21:54:26Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T21:54:26Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Move the verifier core out of the CLI layer, and stop it reading package.json\n\nA build plugin had to import from `src/cli/` to verify its own output, and the\nverifier opened package.json for itself — so the identity it asserted and the\nidentity its caller would write into an archive came from two different reads.\n`verifyBuild` now takes app metadata and peer-derived share expectations as\ninput, from one snapshot its caller already holds, and reads nothing but the\nbuild output. `verifyApp` stays where it was, as the thin wrapper that resolves\npaths and takes that one snapshot.\n\nOne input the design asked for is deliberately absent, and the checklist and\n§6.2 now say so. The configured share block, remote and runtime plugins are read\nfrom mf-manifest.json rather than accepted from the caller, because the build\nembeds them there through `manifest.additionalData` for exactly this purpose,\nand taking them from the plugin instead would hand the verifier the\nconfiguration a build was made with and compare it against itself — which is\nwhat the file''s own opening line, \"verifies on PAYLOAD, not on config\", exists\nto prevent. The asymmetry the review was right about is untouched: the\nstandalone CLI has no build configuration to capture, and does not pretend to.\n\nA corrupt artifact is now a result rather than an exception. `JSON.parse` of\nmf-manifest.json was unguarded, so invalid JSON escaped as a SyntaxError naming\na byte offset — a stack trace that tells a developer neither which file is wrong\nnor what to do. Invalid JSON, null, arrays and non-objects all come back as\nnamed failures, and a child-process test holds the CLI to exit 1, empty stdout,\na bounded stderr diagnostic, and no stack trace.\n\nCheck counts are unchanged from the Phase 0 baseline for all five apps\n(29/18/28/28/28), which is the point: the code moved, the output did not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b1d82a1e3e9cc688ecc6aa98f5a43eba4ebd1b54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/b1d82a1e3e9cc688ecc6aa98f5a43eba4ebd1b54"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/8620fe4cb126d86e53cc4ef2c48e746b84e3cd94","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/8620fe4cb126d86e53cc4ef2c48e746b84e3cd94","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDg2MjBmZTRjYjEyNmQ4NmU1M2NjNGVmMmM0OGU3NDZiODRlM2NkOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/0a14c82bc7b365b3dda0b9923bc6adba4fc86ac0","sha":"0a14c82bc7b365b3dda0b9923bc6adba4fc86ac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/0a14c82bc7b365b3dda0b9923bc6adba4fc86ac0"}],"sha":"8620fe4cb126d86e53cc4ef2c48e746b84e3cd94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/8620fe4cb126d86e53cc4ef2c48e746b84e3cd94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/0a14c82bc7b365b3dda0b9923bc6adba4fc86ac0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T21:26:09Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T21:26:09Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Build the wire format: schema, predicates, corpora, and one serializer\n\nCanonical validity is three things, and a JSON Schema is only one of them. It\nreceives an already-decoded value, so it cannot express email-like author\ndetection, canonical URL serialization, inspection of encoded path components\nbefore a URL parser normalizes them, or SemVer semantics — and a finite corpus\ncannot define an answer for every input either. So the predicates ship as a\nnormative artifact beside the schema, the SDK reads its constants from that\nartifact rather than restating them, and both are pinned in an append-only\n$id-to-digest ledger. A test packs the tarball and re-hashes what is actually\ninside it, because validating the workspace copy proves nothing about the copy\nthe App Store pins.\n\nTwo contracts run through the builder and they are not the same one. Package\nsource forms — an author object, a repository shorthand, an SSH URL — are\nproducer INPUTS. Canonical wire forms are what both sides implement, and every\nsource form is invalid there: a Store that normalized an upload would be\nrewriting a submitted identity. They get two corpora, 46 cases and 39, and the\nwire validator is written so that \"canonical\" means renormalizing changes\nnothing.\n\nThe corpus earned its keep immediately. `https://github.com:443/owner/repo`\npassed the port check, because WHATWG URL silently drops a default port — which\nis exactly the silent stripping the rule exists to forbid. Ports, queries and\nfragments are now read off the raw string, before any parser can normalize them\naway.\n\nSerialization is one function with a fixed field order, two-space indent and one\ntrailing newline, and it enforces the document limit in OCTETS — `maxLength`\ncounts code points of a decoded string, not bytes of a file, so the schema\ncannot do it. The archive copy and the CLI copy are compared byte for byte, and\ntwo callers of JSON.stringify with different spacing would pass an object\ncomparison and fail a real one.\n\nTwo rules reach past the manifest. The reserved-id list is a RUNTIME rule, not a\nsubmission-profile one: the host indexes apps in ordinary prototype-bearing\nrecords, so an app called `toString` reads as already installed and one called\n`__proto__` mutates a record''s prototype. The runtime reader now rejects all\nfourteen names. And the scaffolder''s SemVer pattern was looser than the reader''s\n— it accepted `1.0.0-01`, which scaffolded a project that failed its own first\nbuild. Both copies are asserted against the artifact, because the scaffolder\ncannot import from a package it does not depend on.\n\n`ajv` is a devDependency only, used to check that our schema and our validator\nagree on every corpus case. The runtime package still has no runtime\ndependencies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fd34d5ca6fed5d663839ba39af245d1641e060d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/fd34d5ca6fed5d663839ba39af245d1641e060d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/0a14c82bc7b365b3dda0b9923bc6adba4fc86ac0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/0a14c82bc7b365b3dda0b9923bc6adba4fc86ac0","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDBhMTRjODJiYzdiMzY1YjNkZGEwYjk5MjNiYzZhZGJhNGZjODZhYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4b07432fa74a919f583e881e55c32774f70c4938","sha":"4b07432fa74a919f583e881e55c32774f70c4938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4b07432fa74a919f583e881e55c32774f70c4938"}],"sha":"0a14c82bc7b365b3dda0b9923bc6adba4fc86ac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/0a14c82bc7b365b3dda0b9923bc6adba4fc86ac0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4b07432fa74a919f583e881e55c32774f70c4938/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T20:21:40Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T20:21:40Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Read package.json once, and parse it for two different lifecycles\n\nThe manifest work needs `author`, `license`, `repository` and `homepage`, and\nneeds to reject them when they are malformed. It must not reject them during\n`vite dev`. Those two requirements look compatible until you notice that\n`defineCyWebApp` calls the reader before it knows whether a zip will be built,\nso anything the reader refuses fails an ordinary build over a field the app\nitself never uses.\n\nSeparate types would not have fixed that; separate callers do. `parseAppMeta`\nruns everywhere and validates identity exactly as before, message for message.\n`parseSubmissionMeta` is reached only from packaging and the CLI, and returns\nevery field as `unknown` — judging them belongs to the manifest builder, where a\nbad value can fail packaging without touching a build that packages nothing.\n\nUnderneath both is one `readPackageSnapshot`, because two independent readers\ncannot make the guarantee the packager needs: that the identity it validates,\nthe identity it writes into the archive, and the peers the verifier compares\nagainst all came from the same bytes. `readAppMeta` and `sharedFromPeers` each\nopened the file, so `verifyApp` read it twice and the two could in principle\ndisagree; a test now counts the reads rather than trusting the arrangement.\n\nThe split also stops a coercion from destroying evidence. The runtime path turns\na non-string `description` into `''''`, which is right for the browser bundle and\nleaves a manifest validator nothing to reject. The snapshot keeps the original.\n\n`readAppMeta(root)` stays public and unchanged in behaviour — it is now the\nwrapper, and a test asserts parity with the primitive. `CyWebBlock` gains\noptional `compatibleHostVersions`; `CyWebAppMeta` and `EXPOSED_META_FIELDS` are\nuntouched, so nothing new reaches the browser bundle. A package.json that parses\nto a string, an array or null now says so instead of throwing a TypeError from\nwhichever property access happened to come first.\n\nAll five apps rebuild with byte-identical mf-manifest audit fields and unchanged\nverify counts (29/18/28/28/28).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebbd83f490a2da919bf36046ce2d73186f3db9e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/ebbd83f490a2da919bf36046ce2d73186f3db9e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/4b07432fa74a919f583e881e55c32774f70c4938","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4b07432fa74a919f583e881e55c32774f70c4938","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDRiMDc0MzJmYTc0YTkxOWY1ODNlODgxZTU1YzMyNzc0ZjcwYzQ5Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/f24feb9c5a0dc481b7f659e90ab14dcbc0c264a8","sha":"f24feb9c5a0dc481b7f659e90ab14dcbc0c264a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/f24feb9c5a0dc481b7f659e90ab14dcbc0c264a8"}],"sha":"4b07432fa74a919f583e881e55c32774f70c4938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4b07432fa74a919f583e881e55c32774f70c4938"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/f24feb9c5a0dc481b7f659e90ab14dcbc0c264a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T04:00:49Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T04:00:49Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Close Phase 0: record the decisions, and what the Store actually did\n\nThe baseline was supposed to be bookkeeping. Submitting one archive by hand\nturned it into the strongest evidence this issue has.\n\nA project scaffolded the way a third-party developer would, published on\napps-stage, produced a Store id of `cytoscapewebsubmissiontest` from the display\nname while the bundle exports `CyApp.id` of `submissionTest`. Feed the resulting\ncatalog entry to Cytoscape Web and `loadRemoteApp` logs one console warning and\nreturns undefined: there is now a published app that cannot be installed, and\nthe only reason is the derived id. The failure no longer needs arguing.\n\nMeasuring the published artifact also corrected two of our own assumptions.\nThe Store already publishes at `/web/{id}/{version}/`, already emits a\none-element catalog array the host parser accepts, already republishes the\narchive byte-for-byte, and already sends `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` on the\nmanifest, the entry and a transitive chunk — so adopting `cy-manifest.id` is\nmostly a question of which string goes into a structure that is otherwise\ncorrect. And it serves versioned files with `no-cache, no-store,\nmust-revalidate`, not the long-lived immutable caching §11.13 was written\nagainst, so the revocation policy has to be built around theirs rather than\naround ours. `nosniff`, CORP, and a published `index.html` are recorded as\nmeasurements to ask about, not as demands.\n\nDecisions closed alongside it: the three dependency approvals, and the schema\n`$id` namespace. The design had claimed `cytoscape.org/schema/…`, a path this\nrepository does not control. An `$id` need not resolve, but the stable identity\ncan never change, so it now uses the path GitHub Pages actually serves.\n\nBaseline facts for later phases: per-app verify counts (29/18/28/28/28), and the\nfinding that the five apps emit only .js, .json and .html — so every asset-class\nfixture for the Phase 4 classifier must be synthetic, and no example build can\never cover the allow half of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed57cdf8503cd8451e849eb75be85168ff9d9148","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/ed57cdf8503cd8451e849eb75be85168ff9d9148"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/f24feb9c5a0dc481b7f659e90ab14dcbc0c264a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/f24feb9c5a0dc481b7f659e90ab14dcbc0c264a8","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKGYyNGZlYjljNWEwZGM0ODFiN2Y2NTllOTBhYjE0ZGNiYzBjMjY0YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/65d5367458d264016a54bf2a5e5f127a88d2eb60","sha":"65d5367458d264016a54bf2a5e5f127a88d2eb60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/65d5367458d264016a54bf2a5e5f127a88d2eb60"}],"sha":"f24feb9c5a0dc481b7f659e90ab14dcbc0c264a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/f24feb9c5a0dc481b7f659e90ab14dcbc0c264a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/65d5367458d264016a54bf2a5e5f127a88d2eb60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T07:59:43Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T07:59:43Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Specify cy-manifest.json, the App Store submission manifest\n\nThe App Store''s web bundle form has no application id field: it derives one\nfrom the display name, so `My App` becomes `myapp` and can never equal\n`cyweb.id`. The host registers a remote under the catalog id, loads\n`./AppConfig`, and rejects an app whose exported `CyApp.id` differs — so the\nmismatch surfaces in the user''s browser at install time, long after review.\nEverything the form asks for is already declared once in package.json; the\nbundle simply is not carrying it (#8).\n\ncy-manifest.md is the wire format and the producer contract, at revision 6\nafter five rounds of review. The parts that took the most argument:\n\n  - no `url` — the deployment URL does not exist at submission time, so the\n    manifest carries an archive-relative `entry` and the Store adds the URL it\n    assigned;\n  - a frozen v1 envelope, because an instance carries only `formatVersion` and\n    could not select among several stable schema revisions;\n  - canonical validity is raw-JSON validation plus the pinned schema plus\n    normative semantic predicates — JSON Schema cannot express URL\n    canonicalization or email-like detection, and fixtures cannot define an\n    answer for every input;\n  - [source] and [wire] labels on every rule, so the Store validates canonical\n    manifests rather than running a second npm normalizer over an upload;\n  - a reserved-id list, because a legal JavaScript identifier is not a safe\n    object key: the host indexes apps in prototype-bearing records, where\n    `toString` reads as installed and `__proto__` mutates a prototype;\n  - a bounded version profile — build metadata rejected, numeric identifiers\n    capped — since node-semver compares two distinct large prerelease\n    identifiers as equal and a \"latest\" endpoint cannot break that tie.\n\nThree acceptance gates, not one. The SDK emitting the file closes only the\nproducer gate; #8 closes on Store adoption, and public self-service publication\nis a third decision that v1 answers with curated-only. The manifest is not\nprovenance and not a privilege boundary, and the document says so where someone\nmight otherwise read it that way.\n\ncy-manifest-checklist.md follows app-sdk-checklist.md: seven phases, ordered\nbecause the package snapshot is what makes every later one-snapshot guarantee\nimplementable. cy-manifest-phase0-baseline.md records what the five apps\nactually build today — which turns out to emit only .js, .json and .html, so\nthe asset-class fixtures must be synthetic and only the deny half of the\nclassifier can ever be covered by a real build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"da84681fab283b199cdee4625aed44ad02941c20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/da84681fab283b199cdee4625aed44ad02941c20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/65d5367458d264016a54bf2a5e5f127a88d2eb60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/65d5367458d264016a54bf2a5e5f127a88d2eb60","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDY1ZDUzNjc0NThkMjY0MDE2YTU0YmYyYTVlNWYxMjdhODhkMmViNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/977589ef2a263819d54f45030c47bdad68491b0c","sha":"977589ef2a263819d54f45030c47bdad68491b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/977589ef2a263819d54f45030c47bdad68491b0c"}],"sha":"65d5367458d264016a54bf2a5e5f127a88d2eb60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/65d5367458d264016a54bf2a5e5f127a88d2eb60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/977589ef2a263819d54f45030c47bdad68491b0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:22:55Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:22:55Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Document that npm create can serve a cached scaffolder\n\nA release does not reach anyone who has run the tool before: `npm create`\nmay run a cached copy without checking the registry, so they keep the\nversion they first fetched. Hit while confirming the 0.3.1 port fix --\nthe run used a cached 0.2.0 and produced port 6000, which looked exactly\nlike the fix not working.\n\nThe tell is a line that is absent rather than one that appears: no\n\"not found and will be installed\" means it came from the cache.\ntroubleshooting.md now says that, gives a command that reports which\nversions are actually cached, and lists the three ways round it\n(@latest, --prefer-online, an exact version) plus how to clear it. Each\nwas run as written before being documented.\n\nIt also warns about the trap that nearly produced a wrong conclusion\nhere: pickPort returns the first FREE port, so an occupied 6000 is\nskipped by every version, including ones without the blocked-port fix.\nComparing versions while something holds 6000 measures nothing. Both\nREADMEs point at the entry from the command that triggers it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"745a04b7e4cb69d611d4fc8461f7ddef99f8b84f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/745a04b7e4cb69d611d4fc8461f7ddef99f8b84f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/977589ef2a263819d54f45030c47bdad68491b0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/977589ef2a263819d54f45030c47bdad68491b0c","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDk3NzU4OWVmMmEyNjM4MTlkNTRmNDUwMzBjNDdiZGFkNjg0OTFiMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/27df1910cd29e42431a644e55e8c7e462309458f","sha":"27df1910cd29e42431a644e55e8c7e462309458f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/27df1910cd29e42431a644e55e8c7e462309458f"}],"sha":"977589ef2a263819d54f45030c47bdad68491b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/977589ef2a263819d54f45030c47bdad68491b0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/27df1910cd29e42431a644e55e8c7e462309458f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T00:23:49Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T00:23:49Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"0.3.1: never hand out a port the browser refuses\n\nThe scaffolder''s port search started at 6000. That is X11, and every\nbrowser refuses to load http:// from it -- so a developer who took the\ndefault got a dev server the HOST could not fetch from:\n\n  http://localhost:6000/cyweb-app.json :: net::ERR_UNSAFE_PORT\n\nwhich surfaces as \"Failed to install app from ...: Failed to fetch\".\nThe same sentence a denied local-network permission produces, so the\ntroubleshooting guide sent anyone who hit this to grant a permission\nthat was never the problem.\n\npickPort now skips Chromium''s restricted list, in the fallback path too\n-- returning a blocked port because nothing was free would hand back\nprecisely the one that cannot work. The default is 6001. A port passed\nexplicitly is refused with the symptom named, rather than accepted and\ndiscovered later.\n\nDocs: 23 references across six files moved off 6000. Two of them told\npeople to pass `--port 6000`, which the validator now rejects, so they\nwere broken as written. troubleshooting.md leads with a table splitting\nthe two unrelated causes of \"Failed to fetch\", because the console is\nthe only thing that distinguishes them.\n\napp-runtime has no code change and is republished for its README alone:\nthe npm package page rendered a dev-server banner naming port 6000,\nwhich is the very mistake this release exists to stop. SDK_VERSION and\nthe workspace consumers stay at ^0.3.0 -- a 0.x caret pins the minor, so\nthey already admit 0.3.1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9abb2d0853947f8d289cdf36f86973c6d6c0770b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/9abb2d0853947f8d289cdf36f86973c6d6c0770b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/27df1910cd29e42431a644e55e8c7e462309458f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/27df1910cd29e42431a644e55e8c7e462309458f","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDI3ZGYxOTEwY2QyOWU0MjQzMWE2NDRlNTVlOGM3ZTQ2MjMwOTQ1OGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/19f3a93b9437c469f4621b160bbdb72eb31634a6","sha":"19f3a93b9437c469f4621b160bbdb72eb31634a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/19f3a93b9437c469f4621b160bbdb72eb31634a6"}],"sha":"27df1910cd29e42431a644e55e8c7e462309458f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/27df1910cd29e42431a644e55e8c7e462309458f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/19f3a93b9437c469f4621b160bbdb72eb31634a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T23:35:49Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T23:35:49Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Release 0.3.0: zip as a build option, and a scaffolder that survives a paste\n\nTwo changes reach app developers only through a release, so both go out\ntogether.\n\n`npm run build:zip` makes the App Store archive a per-build decision\nrather than an edit to the one file the SDK tells you not to write.\nCYWEB_APP_ZIP sits underneath it and works in both directions, so an app\nthat commits `appStoreZip: true` can still skip the zip while iterating.\n\nThe scaffolder no longer prompts into a pipe. Pasting the Quick Start''s\nthree-line block fed `cd my-app` and `npm run dev` to the prompts as\nanswers and exited 13 on an unsettled await; a non-TTY stdin now takes\nthe defaults and says so (#6).\n\nVersion, the pin scaffolds emit, all five workspace consumers and the\nlock move together, because they have to: `^0.2.0` does not admit\n0.3.0, and leaving a consumer behind makes npm resolve app-runtime from\nthe REGISTRY while the repository appears to test the new code. That was\nthe 0.2.0 lesson and the guards for it -- the SDK_VERSION test and\n`npm ci` -- both pass here.\n\nTarballs check out: app-runtime 31 files, create-cytoscape-app 58 with\ndist/interactive.js present.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ad73eb0b01e3359d7ae3bb14c7e900357b3f473","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/8ad73eb0b01e3359d7ae3bb14c7e900357b3f473"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/19f3a93b9437c469f4621b160bbdb72eb31634a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/19f3a93b9437c469f4621b160bbdb72eb31634a6","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDE5ZjNhOTNiOTQzN2M0NjlmNDYyMWIxNjBiYmRiNzJlYjMxNjM0YTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/f4bb5df80fe303916169c282791645164d58117c","sha":"f4bb5df80fe303916169c282791645164d58117c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/f4bb5df80fe303916169c282791645164d58117c"}],"sha":"19f3a93b9437c469f4621b160bbdb72eb31634a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/19f3a93b9437c469f4621b160bbdb72eb31634a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/f4bb5df80fe303916169c282791645164d58117c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:46:39Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:46:39Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Take the defaults when stdin is not a terminal (#6)\n\nPasting the Quick Start''s three-line block fed `cd my-app` and `npm run\ndev` to the interactive prompts as ANSWERS, then exited 13 on an\nunsettled top-level await with stdin exhausted. Reproduced on Node 24,\nso this is not a version problem.\n\nThe reporter read it as create-cytoscape-app not being installed. It was\ninstalled and running; nothing in the output said otherwise, which is a\nfair measure of how illegible the failure was.\n\nnpx would not have helped: `npx create-cytoscape-app my-app` is\ninteractive in exactly the same way and fails identically. Nor would\ndocumenting an install step, since the package was never missing.\n\nPrompting into a pipe cannot work, so it no longer tries. `--yes` stays\nthe explicit way in; a non-TTY stdin now takes the same path and says so\non stderr, so a deliberate pipe does not silently lose its answers. The\nrest of a pasted block is then left in the shell''s buffer, where it\nbelongs -- the documented block now runs start to finish.\n\nThe decision is its own module because index.ts runs the CLI at import\ntime, so nothing in it can be imported by a test, and this is the part\nmost worth pinning. Mutation-checked: removing the TTY check fails two\ntests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef785bb1c6c65296b67626fc559a84664dba6035","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/ef785bb1c6c65296b67626fc559a84664dba6035"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/f4bb5df80fe303916169c282791645164d58117c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/f4bb5df80fe303916169c282791645164d58117c","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKGY0YmI1ZGY4MGZlMzAzOTE2MTY5YzI4Mjc5MTY0NTE2NGQ1ODExN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4569df0b81b89df98446a84864d9760e93d8817b","sha":"4569df0b81b89df98446a84864d9760e93d8817b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4569df0b81b89df98446a84864d9760e93d8817b"}],"sha":"f4bb5df80fe303916169c282791645164d58117c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/f4bb5df80fe303916169c282791645164d58117c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4569df0b81b89df98446a84864d9760e93d8817b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:29:18Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:29:18Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Make the App Store zip a build option, not a config edit\n\nProducing a zip meant editing vite.config.ts, which is the one file the\nSDK tells you not to write. It is a per-build decision -- you want an\narchive when you are about to submit one, not on every build -- so it\nnow comes from the command line.\n\nGenerated projects ship `npm run build:zip`. That is the discoverable\nhalf: `npm run` lists it, so neither the config field nor a variable\nname has to be known in advance, and the option going unnoticed is what\nprompted this.\n\nUnderneath it is CYWEB_APP_ZIP, which works in BOTH directions. A\none-way switch would send an app that commits `appStoreZip: true` back\nto editing its config to skip the zip during a quick build -- the exact\nround trip being removed. An unrecognised value turns it on rather than\nfailing: the variable is reached for at the moment someone wants a zip,\nand refusing the build over `CYWEB_APP_ZIP=yes` would fail them for\nbeing right.\n\ncross-env is the one dependency a generated project now carries purely\nfor ergonomics. `VAR=1 cmd` is not valid in cmd.exe, so without it the\nscript would work on two platforms of three, which is worse than not\nshipping it. The host repository already depends on it for the same\nreason.\n\nVerified on a generated project against the workspace SDK: plain build\nwrites no zip, `npm run build:zip` writes one, and CYWEB_APP_ZIP=0\nsuppresses it for an app whose config asks for it. Mutation-checked --\ndropping cross-env from the generated deps fails a test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b67362c7bec137928ee8ae5f27977d115d4eb12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/5b67362c7bec137928ee8ae5f27977d115d4eb12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/4569df0b81b89df98446a84864d9760e93d8817b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4569df0b81b89df98446a84864d9760e93d8817b","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDQ1NjlkZjBiODFiODlkZjk4NDQ2YTg0ODY0ZDk3NjBlOTNkODgxN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/9eb4a1e34593a7f7968fee05b13dbf2969b9deed","sha":"9eb4a1e34593a7f7968fee05b13dbf2969b9deed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/9eb4a1e34593a7f7968fee05b13dbf2969b9deed"}],"sha":"4569df0b81b89df98446a84864d9760e93d8817b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4569df0b81b89df98446a84864d9760e93d8817b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/9eb4a1e34593a7f7968fee05b13dbf2969b9deed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:57:30Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:57:30Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Close the release items: 0.2.0 is the default install and works from it\n\n`latest` now points at 0.2.0 on both packages and 0.1.0 is deprecated as\n\"Superseded by 0.2.0.\" -- which is what npm''s deprecated field is for,\nand the first accurate use of it here.\n\nVerified from an isolated npm cache, running the command the README\nactually gives, with no version specifier: `npm create cytoscape-app`\nresolves 0.2.0, pins ^0.2.0, installs app-runtime 0.2.0, and\nCYWEB_DEV_HOST prints a dev1 install link. Then end to end into the real\ndev1 -- confirmation dialog, remoteEntry.js, the app''s own modules, 13\nrequests reaching the dev server.\n\nThe only deprecation warning left in an install log is cron-parser, a\ntransitive dependency. That is the point: nothing of ours competes with\nit any more, so a reader who sees one has reason to look.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1107f0adb05583d942699ef96aee4a26386cfc10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/1107f0adb05583d942699ef96aee4a26386cfc10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/9eb4a1e34593a7f7968fee05b13dbf2969b9deed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/9eb4a1e34593a7f7968fee05b13dbf2969b9deed","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDllYjRhMWUzNDU5M2E3Zjc5NjhmZWUwNWIxM2RiZjI5NjliOWRlZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4b2469126dfa1fb9669c92673267b3b1efd50c31","sha":"4b2469126dfa1fb9669c92673267b3b1efd50c31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4b2469126dfa1fb9669c92673267b3b1efd50c31"}],"sha":"9eb4a1e34593a7f7968fee05b13dbf2969b9deed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/9eb4a1e34593a7f7968fee05b13dbf2969b9deed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4b2469126dfa1fb9669c92673267b3b1efd50c31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:45:54Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:45:54Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Retire the deprecation notice and the withheld `latest` tag\n\nBoth were the release''s Preview signal. Neither did what it was written\nto do, and the question that exposed it -- whether `deprecated` is\nmisleading -- was the right one to ask.\n\n`deprecated` is npm''s word for superseded or going away. A Preview is\nthe newest thing and is meant to be used. On install the notice appeared\nbeside `cron-parser@4.9.0: v4 is no longer maintained` with nothing to\ntell them apart; dependency tooling treats a deprecated dependency as\nsomething to remediate, which would have flagged app authors for\nfollowing the documentation. It was also the wrong scope: \"no sandbox,\nno signature verification\" is a property of the platform until Theme G\nlands, not of one version, and parking it there spent the one field that\ncould later say \"superseded by x.y.z\".\n\nHolding `latest` back was worse, and only visible once 0.2.0 existed.\n0.1.0 is a Preview with identical security properties, so nothing was\nprotected -- the effect was that `npm install @cytoscape-web/app-runtime`\nand `npm create cytoscape-app`, both of which the README tells people to\nrun, served the build without devHost.js. CYWEB_DEV_HOST did nothing, in\nthe silence this whole feature was written to end. The release had\nshipped without fixing what it was for.\n\nPreview status now rides on 0.x, the package READMEs npm renders on the\npackage page, and the guides -- all rewritten to say what the limit\nactually is rather than to point at an install-time warning. The §3\nhost-side prerequisites still gate 1.0.\n\nTwo dist-tag moves remain; npm dist-tag is not covered by trusted\npublishing, so they are manual and recorded in the checklist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d9f8c38b86a4a836c2c6ef099cf92aee9d7322af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/d9f8c38b86a4a836c2c6ef099cf92aee9d7322af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/4b2469126dfa1fb9669c92673267b3b1efd50c31","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4b2469126dfa1fb9669c92673267b3b1efd50c31","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDRiMjQ2OTEyNmRmYTFmYjk2NjljOTI2NzMyNjdiM2IxZWZkNTBjMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/0f0358cac55e3d4ca01c80f65791f75048c8eadc","sha":"0f0358cac55e3d4ca01c80f65791f75048c8eadc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/0f0358cac55e3d4ca01c80f65791f75048c8eadc"}],"sha":"4b2469126dfa1fb9669c92673267b3b1efd50c31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4b2469126dfa1fb9669c92673267b3b1efd50c31"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/0f0358cac55e3d4ca01c80f65791f75048c8eadc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:32:29Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:32:29Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Stop failing a finished release over a notice CI cannot apply\n\nBoth packages published successfully at 0.2.0, then the run went red on\n`npm deprecate`. Trusted publishing issues a credential scoped to `npm\npublish` and nothing else, so with no NODE_AUTH_TOKEN setup-node writes\nits placeholder into .npmrc and deprecate answers 404. The 0.1.0 release\nmanaged it only because a granular token still existed then, and\nremoving that token was a deliberate trade -- this is the half of it\nthat had not been paid yet.\n\nThe step now prints the two commands and warns, rather than attempting\nthem and failing. A red run on a complete release is worse than a\nmissing notice: it says nothing shipped when everything did.\n\nA read-back step is kept, and still fails if a version is genuinely\nabsent from the registry. Only the notice is downgraded to a warning,\nbecause it is the one thing this job cannot do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9a700adf8feddb63c847b6507a6289a6cdd1dde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/f9a700adf8feddb63c847b6507a6289a6cdd1dde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/0f0358cac55e3d4ca01c80f65791f75048c8eadc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/0f0358cac55e3d4ca01c80f65791f75048c8eadc","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDBmMDM1OGNhYzU1ZTNkNGNhMDFjODBmNjU3OTFmNzUwNDhjOGVhZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/10e22b4305785458fc71f71ee5afc1096e0d2ce8","sha":"10e22b4305785458fc71f71ee5afc1096e0d2ce8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/10e22b4305785458fc71f71ee5afc1096e0d2ce8"}],"sha":"0f0358cac55e3d4ca01c80f65791f75048c8eadc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/0f0358cac55e3d4ca01c80f65791f75048c8eadc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/10e22b4305785458fc71f71ee5afc1096e0d2ce8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:18:11Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:18:11Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Let the scaffold job test the SDK it is about to publish\n\nRaising SDK_VERSION to ^0.2.0 made CI demand a publish that CI itself\nwas blocking. The scaffold job resolves @cytoscape-web/app-runtime from\nnpm, deliberately, because that is what a generated project depends on\n-- but on the commit that raises the pin, the version scaffolds ask for\ndoes not exist on the registry yet, and it cannot until this job passes.\n\nThe job now checks whether the pinned range resolves. Normally it does\nand nothing changes. On a version-bump commit it does not, and the job\ninstalls the app-runtime tarball it already packs a few lines earlier.\nThat is the same intent at a different moment rather than an exception\nto it: what a user gets after the release is exactly that tarball.\n\nThe fallback logs through ::notice:: rather than passing quietly,\nbecause a publish that simply failed looks identical from inside this\njob, and that one should not be waved through.\n\nRehearsed locally end to end: scaffold panel from the packed scaffolder,\nfall back to the tarball, then build, `cyweb-app verify` (27 checks),\ntypecheck and test all pass in the generated project.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"daadc90e8b2c2eed06b53271ca03d495a5faa87c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/daadc90e8b2c2eed06b53271ca03d495a5faa87c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/10e22b4305785458fc71f71ee5afc1096e0d2ce8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/10e22b4305785458fc71f71ee5afc1096e0d2ce8","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDEwZTIyYjQzMDU3ODU0NThmYzcxZjcxZWU1YWZjMTA5NmUwZDJjZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/6d2571a77222bfae9bb41cb9af24b4d23da61bc4","sha":"6d2571a77222bfae9bb41cb9af24b4d23da61bc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/6d2571a77222bfae9bb41cb9af24b4d23da61bc4"}],"sha":"10e22b4305785458fc71f71ee5afc1096e0d2ce8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/10e22b4305785458fc71f71ee5afc1096e0d2ce8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/6d2571a77222bfae9bb41cb9af24b4d23da61bc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:14:29Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:14:29Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Carry the 0.2.0 bump into the workspace consumers and the lock file\n\nThe release rehearsal failed at `npm ci`: package-lock.json still\nrecorded app-runtime 0.1.0. Bumping a workspace package''s version is not\na local edit -- every consumer''s range has to move with it, and the lock\nhas to be regenerated, or the tree no longer describes itself.\n\nWorse than a stale lock, and the reason this needed care rather than a\nquick `npm install`: all five example apps declared `^0.1.0`, which a\n0.2.0 workspace no longer satisfies. Regenerating the lock without\ntouching them made npm resolve app-runtime from the REGISTRY instead of\nthe workspace -- so the repository would have built and verified against\nthe published 0.1.0 while appearing to test the new code. The ranges are\nnow ^0.2.0, matching SDK_VERSION, and the lock links the workspace again\n(zero registry entries for app-runtime).\n\nThe lock diff is seven lines, all of them this bump. Nothing else was\nallowed to drift in.\n\nProcess note: this class of failure was already guarded. ci.yml runs\n`npm ci` in five jobs -- but only on push to main/development or on a\nPR, so a feature branch does not trigger it, and dispatching the release\nworkflow straight from the branch reached npm ci with no earlier warning\nand burned an environment approval. Merging before releasing is what\nputs the guard back in front.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab5694a862bd6ecf696eae94cc8c15295b145dbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/ab5694a862bd6ecf696eae94cc8c15295b145dbe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/6d2571a77222bfae9bb41cb9af24b4d23da61bc4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/6d2571a77222bfae9bb41cb9af24b4d23da61bc4","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDZkMjU3MWE3NzIyMmJmYWU5YmI0MWNiOWFmMjRiNGQyM2RhNjFiYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4f5ed2d6604ce6e5a53d9ee829409e5d4c745ba8","sha":"4f5ed2d6604ce6e5a53d9ee829409e5d4c745ba8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4f5ed2d6604ce6e5a53d9ee829409e5d4c745ba8"}],"sha":"6d2571a77222bfae9bb41cb9af24b4d23da61bc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/6d2571a77222bfae9bb41cb9af24b4d23da61bc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4f5ed2d6604ce6e5a53d9ee829409e5d4c745ba8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:27:08Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:27:08Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Prepare 0.2.0, and make the version coupling a test rather than a habit\n\nThe documentation described CYWEB_DEV_HOST while every scaffolded app\nstill resolved app-runtime 0.1.0, which has no devHost.js and ignores\nthe variable silently -- no error, only a dev-server banner naming the\nwrong host. Both packages go to 0.2.0 and SDK_VERSION to ^0.2.0 in this\none change, because a 0.x caret pins the minor: ^0.1.0 cannot resolve\n0.2.0, so bumping the runtime alone would have left new projects exactly\nwhere they were while looking like a release.\n\nA test now enforces that rather than a comment asking someone to\nremember: SDK_VERSION must admit the app-runtime version in the\nworkspace, and it fails with the instruction instead of a bare version\nmismatch. Mutation-checked by putting ^0.1.0 back.\n\nVerified against the tarballs rather than the source tree, since `files`\nis an allowlist and a missing entry produces a package that installs and\nthen fails at use: devHost.js is in the app-runtime tarball, both\ntarballs are 0.2.0, and a project scaffolded from the built scaffolder\npins ^0.2.0.\n\nThe docs now state the requirement as a version rather than as \"not\nreleased yet\", which is true both before and after publishing.\n\nNothing is published by this commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18887f1c0cb36559692a85a2fca7c6fd822abad8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/18887f1c0cb36559692a85a2fca7c6fd822abad8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/4f5ed2d6604ce6e5a53d9ee829409e5d4c745ba8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/4f5ed2d6604ce6e5a53d9ee829409e5d4c745ba8","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDRmNWVkMmQ2NjA0Y2U2ZTVhNTNkOWVlODI5NDA5ZTVkNGM3NDViYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/1f2156e3fa285a6327f5389eff26681be5a3cbce","sha":"1f2156e3fa285a6327f5389eff26681be5a3cbce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/1f2156e3fa285a6327f5389eff26681be5a3cbce"}],"sha":"4f5ed2d6604ce6e5a53d9ee829409e5d4c745ba8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/4f5ed2d6604ce6e5a53d9ee829409e5d4c745ba8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/1f2156e3fa285a6327f5389eff26681be5a3cbce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:19:59Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:19:59Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Close H-5 and G-6 on the roadmap, and record what Phase 6 uncovered\n\nBoth landed in cytoscape-web PR #677 and dev1 is running them, so the\nroadmap stops describing them as future work. G-6''s acceptance\nconstraint is recorded as verified rather than promised, along with the\ntwo things it turned on that were not visible from the plan: the gate\nkeys on provenance rather than origin, because apps.json serves the\nbundled apps from an origin the allow-list does not name; and stored\nAppSource is not that provenance, because reconcileInstalledStatus\nstamps ''manifest'' whichever manifest an entry came from.\n\nH-1 stays open, and the roadmap now says H-5 did not need it after all.\nThe plan assumed a runtime config.json was a prerequisite, since a\nbuild-time flag set for dev1 would also be set for production. Making\nthe opt-in name the origin it applies to removed that coupling. H-1\nremains worth doing for the organizational-catalog items.\n\nPhase 6 also uncovered work rather than only completing it: the docs now\ndescribe a capability that is not in any published release. The\npublished app-runtime 0.1.0 has no devHost.js and create-cytoscape-app\npins ^0.1.0, so a newly scaffolded app ignores CYWEB_DEV_HOST silently.\nThat is logged as an open item, including that SDK_VERSION has to be\nbumped in the same change because ^0.1.0 would not admit a 0.2.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"729e4666f65046c88065d1b45a913132298085b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/729e4666f65046c88065d1b45a913132298085b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/1f2156e3fa285a6327f5389eff26681be5a3cbce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/1f2156e3fa285a6327f5389eff26681be5a3cbce","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDFmMjE1NmUzZmEyODVhNjMyN2Y1Mzg5ZWZmMjY2ODFiZTVhM2NiY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/294e84f4e9c7989fe80093bf96de30413490252c","sha":"294e84f4e9c7989fe80093bf96de30413490252c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/294e84f4e9c7989fe80093bf96de30413490252c"}],"sha":"1f2156e3fa285a6327f5389eff26681be5a3cbce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/1f2156e3fa285a6327f5389eff26681be5a3cbce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/294e84f4e9c7989fe80093bf96de30413490252c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:19:39Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:19:39Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Document developing against a shared host, and the symptom when it fails\n\ngetting-started said this could not be done and named the roadmap items\nthat would fix it. Those landed and dev1 is running them, so the note is\nreplaced by a new section 5d rather than folded into 5c: checking a\ndeployed app against a real host and developing against one are\ndifferent activities, and 5c was already about the first.\n\nThe browser prompt is reproduced in its own words rather than as a\nscreenshot -- the guides carry no images, and the wording is the whole\npoint, so keeping it as text keeps it greppable. Its wording mentions\nneither localhost nor dev servers, because it is written for the case it\nnormally guards against, so the correct answer looks like the unsafe\none and the guide says plainly to click Allow.\n\nWhat most needed writing down is the failure. A developer who denies the\nprompt, or who blocked it long ago for the unrelated Cytoscape Desktop\nintegration that raises the same prompt on this host, sees only \"Failed\nto fetch\" -- which names neither the permission nor the fix, and the\ndecision is remembered per site rather than per port so it persists.\nThat symptom is now named in 5d and carries its own troubleshooting.md\nRuntime Errors entry, which is where someone already stuck will look.\n\nTwo claims are narrower than the plan called for, both deliberately.\nThe flow was measured on Chrome; Edge shares the engine but was not\ntested, and the guide says exactly that. And production is named as not\nthis yet, on a re-measurement rather than a repeat: web.cytoscape.org is\nstill the Webpack build, so an app built with this toolchain resolves no\nexports against it and fails silently.\n\nThe README offers the flow too, since removing the host checkout is the\nbarrier-to-entry improvement this work exists for. Both documents carry\nthe version caveat found while checking that a scaffolded app can\nactually do this: the published app-runtime 0.1.0 has no devHost.js and\ncreate-cytoscape-app pins ^0.1.0, so a new scaffold ignores\nCYWEB_DEV_HOST silently. Naming that symptom is the most a document can\ndo; a release is what fixes it.\n\nAlso corrects the banner text quoted in both files, which still showed\n\"Install it into a local host:\" after the dev server stopped printing it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70b5d19c8ae970a7dec0c7abcd07abf5f4f6b806","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/70b5d19c8ae970a7dec0c7abcd07abf5f4f6b806"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/294e84f4e9c7989fe80093bf96de30413490252c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/294e84f4e9c7989fe80093bf96de30413490252c","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDI5NGU4NGY0ZTljNzk4OWZlODAwOTNiZjk2ZGUzMDQxMzQ5MDI1MmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/033bc6097b0849516245f22b61a8a9ef617c3364","sha":"033bc6097b0849516245f22b61a8a9ef617c3364","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/033bc6097b0849516245f22b61a8a9ef617c3364"}],"sha":"294e84f4e9c7989fe80093bf96de30413490252c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/294e84f4e9c7989fe80093bf96de30413490252c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/033bc6097b0849516245f22b61a8a9ef617c3364/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T08:21:08Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T08:21:08Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Record Phases 4 and 5, including what Phase 5 could not verify\n\nPhase 5 was meant to run the whole flow against dev1. It cannot: the\nbranch is not merged into development, dev1 tracks development, and none\nof dev1''s served bundles contain allowsLocalhostAppsOn. A test there\nwould fail for a reason unrelated to the code.\n\nSo the flow was verified against a host on this machine''s LAN address\ninstead, which makes hostIsLocalhost false and leaves the opt-in as the\nonly way through. That covers the host gate end to end in a real\nbrowser: with the opt-in naming the host''s own origin the app server\nreceived the manifest request, then remoteEntry.js, then the app''s own\nmodules; with it naming a different deployment there was no confirmation\ndialog and remoteEntry.js was never requested at all.\n\nTwo things are recorded as not verified rather than glossed. dev1 itself\nis blocked on a merge and a deploy. And the browser permission was never\nexercised: a private LAN address was expected to make loopback a more\nprivate space, and it does not -- with the permission denied the install\nstill succeeded. The restriction measured in Phase 0 is public to\nloopback, so only a genuinely public origin can cover that layer. The\nreproduction therefore covers the host gate thoroughly and the browser\nlayer not at all.\n\nAlso recorded: Keycloak stops this flow on an unregistered origin, with\na 400 on the redirect_uri and a symptom that names neither Keycloak nor\nthe cause. Anyone reproducing this locally hits that wall first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b991b753900daf39e3b8919a44764d0176a88d00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/b991b753900daf39e3b8919a44764d0176a88d00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/033bc6097b0849516245f22b61a8a9ef617c3364","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/033bc6097b0849516245f22b61a8a9ef617c3364","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDAzM2JjNjA5N2IwODQ5NTE2MjQ1ZjIyYjYxYThhOWVmNjE3YzMzNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/d937ce4090cee9ecda50ff898c7cb7db1acbb2d6","sha":"d937ce4090cee9ecda50ff898c7cb7db1acbb2d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/d937ce4090cee9ecda50ff898c7cb7db1acbb2d6"}],"sha":"033bc6097b0849516245f22b61a8a9ef617c3364","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/033bc6097b0849516245f22b61a8a9ef617c3364"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/d937ce4090cee9ecda50ff898c7cb7db1acbb2d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T08:20:52Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T08:20:52Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Let CYWEB_DEV_HOST point a dev session at another host\n\nThe host an app is developed against is a property of the session, not\nof the app, so it now comes from the environment rather than a committed\nconfig field:\n\n    CYWEB_DEV_HOST=https://dev1.ndexbio.org/cytoscape npm run dev\n\nBoth the printed install link and the host remoteEntry.js the app loads\ncome from one resolution. Redirecting only the link would leave the app\nrunning against the local host while telling the developer it was\nsomewhere else -- the class of silent mismatch this package exists to\ncatch. For the same reason the variable is refused rather than merged\nwhen it is combined with an explicit devHostRemoteEntryUrl, and a value\nthat is not an absolute http(s) URL fails the build instead of being\nignored.\n\nTrailing slashes are normalized in both directions, which is not\ncosmetic. Too many and the derived entry doubles into\n`/cytoscape//remoteEntry.js`; too few and the install link is\n`/cytoscape?installApp=...`, which dev1 answers with a 301 -- harmless\nthere because Apache preserves the query, but this is the one link a\ndeveloper is told to open and not every server preserves a query string\nacross a directory redirect. Both forms were measured against dev1.\n\nThe banner names the host, marks it with (CYWEB_DEV_HOST) when the\nvariable chose it, and adds the browser''s local-network prompt in the\nprompt''s own words, since that wording mentions neither localhost nor\ndev servers. The note appears only for an off-loopback host: a localhost\nhost reaching a localhost app crosses no address-space boundary, so it\nwould be noise on the common path.\n\nWith the variable unset, behaviour is unchanged -- the property the\ntests pin first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"28f6328ca5e135cb098bc321041c2720080c8eae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/28f6328ca5e135cb098bc321041c2720080c8eae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/d937ce4090cee9ecda50ff898c7cb7db1acbb2d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/d937ce4090cee9ecda50ff898c7cb7db1acbb2d6","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKGQ5MzdjZTQwOTBjZWU5ZWNkYTUwZmY4OThjN2NiN2RiMWFjYmIyZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/ac1d0a1d32e1b4c0927543a3b236b675246671d7","sha":"ac1d0a1d32e1b4c0927543a3b236b675246671d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/ac1d0a1d32e1b4c0927543a3b236b675246671d7"}],"sha":"d937ce4090cee9ecda50ff898c7cb7db1acbb2d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/d937ce4090cee9ecda50ff898c7cb7db1acbb2d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/ac1d0a1d32e1b4c0927543a3b236b675246671d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T05:47:52Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T05:47:52Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Mark Phase 3 done, and record why the obvious fix was wrong\n\nThe plan treated the catalog bypass as a check that was simply missing.\nMeasuring it during implementation showed the naive fix would disable\nevery app the product ships with: apps.json serves them from\ncytoscape.org and the install allow-list names apps.cytoscape.org. That\nis now written down, along with the provenance-based rule that replaces\nit, so the next reader does not rediscover it by breaking production.\n\nAlso records two things the checklist did not previously distinguish:\nthe startup auto-load needs the gate on its own account, because it\nresolves through the catalog rather than the installed record; and the\nexisting e2e cases prove local development still works but prove nothing\nabout the bypass, since host and app are both on localhost there. A new\ne2e covers the refusal directly.\n\nOne gap is stated rather than papered over: \"the default catalog keeps\nworking\" is verified at the unit level only, because no e2e activates a\nbundled app. The release note for the behaviour change stays open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae5dc85b7fd9bea153547d9fde9ba67b79aaf044","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/ae5dc85b7fd9bea153547d9fde9ba67b79aaf044"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/ac1d0a1d32e1b4c0927543a3b236b675246671d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/ac1d0a1d32e1b4c0927543a3b236b675246671d7","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKGFjMWQwYTFkMzJlMWI0YzA5Mjc1NDNhM2IyMzZiNjc1MjQ2NjcxZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/7d993b1bbca1f9b279104deba96baac817db6731","sha":"7d993b1bbca1f9b279104deba96baac817db6731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/7d993b1bbca1f9b279104deba96baac817db6731"}],"sha":"ac1d0a1d32e1b4c0927543a3b236b675246671d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/ac1d0a1d32e1b4c0927543a3b236b675246671d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/7d993b1bbca1f9b279104deba96baac817db6731/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T02:07:33Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T02:07:33Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Mark Phase 2 done in the remote-dev-host checklist\n\nRecords what the phase actually found rather than what it planned: the\nopt-in reaches five wirings, not four, because validateManifestUrl is a\nsecond localhost check with its own isDev test and would have left the\nManifest Source path broken on dev1 after everything else shipped.\n\nAlso records how the wiring tests were shown not to be vacuous -- each\ncall site was mutated and its test confirmed to fail -- and notes that\ndev1 still cannot reach this: the catalog path it uses today remains the\nunchecked bypass Phase 3 closes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79ef8da12e0d1a55e6296b6a78db6e1e831a6f45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/79ef8da12e0d1a55e6296b6a78db6e1e831a6f45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/7d993b1bbca1f9b279104deba96baac817db6731","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/7d993b1bbca1f9b279104deba96baac817db6731","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDdkOTkzYjFiYmNhMWY5YjI3OTEwNGRlYmE5NmJhYWM4MTdkYjY3MzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/479e1b2f6f4de941fd8238bea6b0caae78ad40ad","sha":"479e1b2f6f4de941fd8238bea6b0caae78ad40ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/479e1b2f6f4de941fd8238bea6b0caae78ad40ad"}],"sha":"7d993b1bbca1f9b279104deba96baac817db6731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/7d993b1bbca1f9b279104deba96baac817db6731"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/479e1b2f6f4de941fd8238bea6b0caae78ad40ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:35:37Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:35:37Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Add the remote-dev-host checklist, with Phase 0 measured and Phase 1 done\n\nGoal, in two stages: dev1 + a developer''s localhost as a supported\ndevelopment environment, then the same for production once it runs the\nVite build. Phase 0 measured the premises rather than assuming them, and\nthree measurements changed the plan.\n\nThe blocker was not where the roadmap put it. Chrome refuses public ->\nloopback requests before the host''s code is consulted at all, and no\nserver header helps because nothing is sent. It is a user permission,\ndefault state \"prompt\", and granting it makes the request succeed --\nverified in headed Chrome, where an ungranted request hangs waiting on\nthe prompt rather than failing. Gesture and no-gesture hang identically,\nso the boot-time ?installApp= fetch can raise the prompt and the SDK''s\nbanner design stands.\n\nThe prompt already fires on dev1 today: useFeatureAvailabilityPolling\npolls 127.0.0.1:1234 every five seconds looking for Cytoscape Desktop.\nSo this project documents an existing condition rather than introducing\none -- and inherits a trap, since a stale Block is remembered per origin\nand would make app installs hang with nothing naming the cause. The host\nalready explains this prompt in CytoscapeDesktopPermissionDialog; later\nphases should reuse that rather than write a second explanation.\n\nThe default/override direction is the opposite of what the plan first\nassumed. The committed config.json is dev1''s, and production is produced\nby hand-editing five documented fields -- a list that would not have\nmentioned a new opt-in. Hence decision D-2, an origin-scoped value that\ncancels itself when copied, and D-1, which keeps Phase 1 to the\napp-install policy instead of the full config migration: the policy\nreaches all four gates through AppConfigContext from a single provider,\nso nothing in the pre-React boot path needs to change.\n\nPhase 1 is complete apart from two items held pending a team decision\nabout config.dev.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8abbc24c11cdd4326ad84cb7a6029c3979ffded1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/8abbc24c11cdd4326ad84cb7a6029c3979ffded1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/479e1b2f6f4de941fd8238bea6b0caae78ad40ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/479e1b2f6f4de941fd8238bea6b0caae78ad40ad","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDQ3OWUxYjJmNmY0ZGU5NDFmZDgyMzhiZWE2YjBjYWFlNzhhZDQwYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/b94bda4654e3c4253cc055963b3fedaab89da8aa","sha":"b94bda4654e3c4253cc055963b3fedaab89da8aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/b94bda4654e3c4253cc055963b3fedaab89da8aa"}],"sha":"479e1b2f6f4de941fd8238bea6b0caae78ad40ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/479e1b2f6f4de941fd8238bea6b0caae78ad40ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/b94bda4654e3c4253cc055963b3fedaab89da8aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T09:34:15Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T09:34:15Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Document dev1 for the job it can do, and record why it cannot do the other one\n\ndev1.ndexbio.org/cytoscape is intended as a recommended host for app developers.\nMeasuring what it can actually support today split that into two jobs, and only\none of them is documentable.\n\nWhat works, and is now in the getting-started guide: verifying a DEPLOYED app\nagainst it. dev1 is a Vite + MF build served by Apache over HTTPS from the\nsubpath /cytoscape/, which makes it the only environment that exercises three\nthings localhost cannot — real HTTPS and MIME types, cross-origin loading of\nevery transitive chunk, and a base path that is not \"/\". A bug that drops or\ndoubles that segment is invisible on localhost and fatal in production.\n\nWhat does not work, and is now roadmap H-5: dev1 as the host for an app on the\ndeveloper''s localhost. The allow-list is an EXACT origin match including the\nport —\n\n  if (allowedOrigins.includes(parsed.origin)) return true\n  return hostIsLocalhost && urlIsLocalhost\n\n— so \"localhost on any port\" cannot be expressed at all, and the scaffolder\npicks the first free port from 6000, which differs per developer and per app.\nEnumerating ports is not a configuration. The fix is a policy change rather than\na longer list: one boolean, `(hostIsLocalhost || allowsLocalhostApps) &&\nurlIsLocalhost`.\n\nThat route DOES work today, but only through the G-6 bypass — Manifest Source\nreaches activateApp, which skips the origin check. So it joins the\norganizational catalog as a second configuration the G-6 fix must not quietly\nremove, and the acceptance constraint under G-6 now names both. Documenting it\nas a recommended workflow would have meant publishing a procedure that depends\non a hole we intend to close.\n\nClosed as a side effect: the vite-migration checklist''s Phase 8 had been waiting\nsince 8/5 on a deployed host publishing window.__CYWEB_HOST__, with the\nbased-urlBaseName branch covered only by a unit test. `npm run preflight:host --\nhttps://dev1.ndexbio.org/cytoscape` passes 10/10, and the descriptor carries\n/cytoscape/ exactly once. Three of that section''s four open items are closed;\nthe fourth is about the apps, not the host.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d2b8d69657ba8965e056d577354a292fb5d6697","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/8d2b8d69657ba8965e056d577354a292fb5d6697"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/b94bda4654e3c4253cc055963b3fedaab89da8aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/b94bda4654e3c4253cc055963b3fedaab89da8aa","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKGI5NGJkYTQ2NTRlM2M0MjUzY2MwNTU5NjNiM2ZlZGFhYjg5ZGE4YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/e87205a5f4fd0cf4509ea3e7b9ab06e525fa967c","sha":"e87205a5f4fd0cf4509ea3e7b9ab06e525fa967c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/e87205a5f4fd0cf4509ea3e7b9ab06e525fa967c"}],"sha":"b94bda4654e3c4253cc055963b3fedaab89da8aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/b94bda4654e3c4253cc055963b3fedaab89da8aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/e87205a5f4fd0cf4509ea3e7b9ab06e525fa967c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T08:33:32Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T08:33:32Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Rewrite the entry documentation around the SDK, and say Preview at the top\n\nThe README opened on a flow for people working on this repository — clone two\nrepos, run five example apps — when the repository exists for people building\none. It now opens with `npm create cytoscape-app`, and the contributor flow is a\nclearly-labelled section further down rather than the front door.\n\nOne section was not merely stale but actively harmful. \"App Entry Point\" taught\n\n  import packageJson from ''../package.json''\n\nwhich is the anti-pattern Phase 3 removed from every app and which\n`cyweb-app verify` now FAILS a build for. Someone following the README would\nhave written code the toolchain rejects. It reads from virtual:cyweb-app-meta\nnow, with a comment saying why.\n\nThe Preview status is stated at the top, above everything, because npm prints a\ndeprecation notice on install and an unexplained one reads as \"abandoned\"\nrather than \"deliberately not ready\". It says what the notice means, that an app\nruns with the host''s full privileges and no sandbox, and — the part that matters\nto someone deciding whether to publish — that asking others to install their app\nasks the same of them.\n\nThe guides and the published site are in the same commit rather than after it.\nFixing the README alone would have left its own Documentation Map pointing at\nguides that still described editing apps.local.json and registering\nsrc/mfRuntimePlugin.ts — a file that exists in no app. That is moving drift, not\nremoving it. architecture-overview now describes the three install routes that\nactually exist, troubleshooting''s \"container missing\" fix points at the single\ncyweb block instead of a three-way manual match, and docs/index.html leads with\nthe generator.\n\nThree references to the old flow survive on purpose: the contributor section,\nand the by-hand `cp -r project-template` alternative in two places. Both are\nstill true.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9c36fabf7e397274d0a4ef6b2bb0e56879586d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/e9c36fabf7e397274d0a4ef6b2bb0e56879586d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/e87205a5f4fd0cf4509ea3e7b9ab06e525fa967c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/e87205a5f4fd0cf4509ea3e7b9ab06e525fa967c","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKGU4NzIwNWE1ZjRmZDBjZjQ1MDllYTNlN2I5YWIwNmU1MjVmYTk2N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/abeecd924ec56b77abd5237227ccee511f136fcf","sha":"abeecd924ec56b77abd5237227ccee511f136fcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/abeecd924ec56b77abd5237227ccee511f136fcf"}],"sha":"e87205a5f4fd0cf4509ea3e7b9ab06e525fa967c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/e87205a5f4fd0cf4509ea3e7b9ab06e525fa967c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/abeecd924ec56b77abd5237227ccee511f136fcf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:48:45Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:48:45Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Build the SDK before typechecking and testing in CI\n\nThe Typecheck and Test jobs have been red since Phase 1 and I did not look.\nBoth run `npm ci` and go straight to their command; neither builds. The apps\nresolve @cytoscape-web/app-runtime through a workspace link, but what they\nimport is its dist/ — `./vite` for the config, `./meta` for the virtual-module\ndeclarations — so a link with nothing built is a directory with no entry points:\n\n  error TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for ''@cytoscape-web/app-runtime/meta''\n  ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: .../app-runtime/dist/vite/index.js\n\nBuild & verify and Scaffold & verify stayed green throughout, because both build\nfirst. Exactly the two jobs that skip the build were failing, consistently, for\ndays.\n\nReproduced locally before fixing rather than reasoned about: deleting the dist\ndirectories makes `npm run typecheck --workspaces` exit 2 with that same TS2688,\nand `npm run build:sdk` first makes it exit 0. build:sdk rather than build —\nonly the two packages are needed, not five app bundles.\n\nWorth naming why this went unnoticed for so long: every phase ended with a local\ngreen battery, and a local checkout always has a built dist/. The signal that\nwould have caught it was CI, which I never opened while the release workflow had\nmy attention. Passing locally is not the same claim as passing in CI, and I was\nreporting the first as if it were the second.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bed7deee02be21a1cfd8f8b36a79a4d3005d4c8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/bed7deee02be21a1cfd8f8b36a79a4d3005d4c8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/abeecd924ec56b77abd5237227ccee511f136fcf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/abeecd924ec56b77abd5237227ccee511f136fcf","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKGFiZWVjZDkyNGVjNTZiNzdhYmQ1MjM3MjI3Y2NlZTUxMWYxMzZmY2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/850da34f94c287b9e1b46b04c3a489900ee708bf","sha":"850da34f94c287b9e1b46b04c3a489900ee708bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/850da34f94c287b9e1b46b04c3a489900ee708bf"}],"sha":"abeecd924ec56b77abd5237227ccee511f136fcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/abeecd924ec56b77abd5237227ccee511f136fcf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/850da34f94c287b9e1b46b04c3a489900ee708bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:15:43Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:15:43Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Phase 6 complete: docs lead with the generator, CI drops the pre-publication hack\n\nBoth packages are on npm. The entry documents now open with\n\n  npm create cytoscape-app my-app\n\ninstead of `cp -r project-template`, and the copy route stays documented as the\nby-hand alternative rather than the default. project-template''s own README says\nwhat it is now: the worked example the generator''s `full` template is built from.\n\nCI installs the SDK from npm rather than rewriting the generated dependency to a\npacked tarball. One asymmetry stays and is spelled out: the SCAFFOLDER is still\ninstalled from its tarball, because a change to it in a PR is exactly what that\njob exists to test, while the SDK is the published one because that is what a\ngenerated project depends on. The SDK is still packed there — `npm pack` runs\nprepack, so a broken build or a stale `files` entry fails in CI rather than at\nrelease time.\n\nThe checklist records the release as it happened. Five attempts, and four of the\nfive failures could not have been caught by the checks in place: a missing\n`repository` field that only the registry validates, a `latest` tag that cannot\nbe withheld at all, `--access public` needed on an unscoped package under\nprovenance, and two publishes silently skipped because output names derived with\n`tr -c` also converted echo''s trailing newline. Only the 403 was predicted.\n\nThe shape they share is worth keeping: a check that does not run, and a\nsubstitution that matches nothing, both look exactly like success.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6209c28c325a06f57c9c3377f27d446e8e1d7daf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/6209c28c325a06f57c9c3377f27d446e8e1d7daf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/850da34f94c287b9e1b46b04c3a489900ee708bf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/850da34f94c287b9e1b46b04c3a489900ee708bf","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDg1MGRhMzRmOTRjMjg3YjllMWI0NmIwNGMzYTQ4OTkwMGVlNzA4YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/9916c71aecd678f172184c265e9875cb7a5df352","sha":"9916c71aecd678f172184c265e9875cb7a5df352","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/9916c71aecd678f172184c265e9875cb7a5df352"}],"sha":"850da34f94c287b9e1b46b04c3a489900ee708bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/850da34f94c287b9e1b46b04c3a489900ee708bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/9916c71aecd678f172184c265e9875cb7a5df352/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:08:27Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:08:27Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Record the OIDC switch and its unverifiable step in the runbook\n\nThe paragraph the previous commit meant to extend had been reflowed, so the\nreplacement silently matched nothing and only the workflow changed. Same class\nof mistake as the output-name bug: a substitution that finds nothing is not an\nerror, so it looks like success.\n\nSays what could not be checked before the token was deleted — a dry run never\nauthenticates, so OIDC is unproven until the next real publish — and where to\nlook if that publish returns a 401.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"74e8525a5e022f278f5edd5d1579f60e43e2025e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/74e8525a5e022f278f5edd5d1579f60e43e2025e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/9916c71aecd678f172184c265e9875cb7a5df352","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/9916c71aecd678f172184c265e9875cb7a5df352","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDk5MTZjNzFhZWNkNjc4ZjE3MjE4NGMyNjVlOTg3NWNiN2E1ZGYzNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/fc5a92df083adf2fc30e45b3334f1a43a939d4a9","sha":"fc5a92df083adf2fc30e45b3334f1a43a939d4a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/fc5a92df083adf2fc30e45b3334f1a43a939d4a9"}],"sha":"9916c71aecd678f172184c265e9875cb7a5df352","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/9916c71aecd678f172184c265e9875cb7a5df352"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/fc5a92df083adf2fc30e45b3334f1a43a939d4a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:07:46Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:07:46Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Switch the release workflow to OIDC: no token anywhere\n\nTrusted publishing is configured on both packages, so the publish and deprecate\nsteps no longer carry NODE_AUTH_TOKEN and no NPM_TOKEN secret is referenced.\n0.1.0 needed one — a trusted publisher is configured on a package''s settings\npage, which exists only once the package has been published, so the first\nrelease could not use OIDC — and it is revoked now that both packages exist.\n\nThe environment name in the npm-side configuration is what binds the trust to a\nREVIEWED run rather than to any run of this workflow. The prerequisite comment\nsays so, because it is the field most likely to be dropped as \"optional\".\n\nWhat could not be verified before removing the token, recorded rather than\nglossed: a dry run never contacts the registry, so it never authenticates, and\nOIDC stays unproven until the next real publish. Removing the token anyway is\nthe right trade — a failed release is recoverable by making a new token, while a\nlive All-Packages credential is a standing risk with a seven-day expiry.\n\nOne thing to expect if that release does fail: setup-node''s registry-url writes\n`_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}` into .npmrc, and with the variable gone that is\nan empty token, which npm may read as \"credentials present but wrong\" rather\nthan falling back to OIDC. A 401 points there first. Noted in the workflow and\nthe runbook so the next person does not rediscover it under time pressure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc34fe8bae617c9c6a251a3fd91eef5f5fdeb805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/dc34fe8bae617c9c6a251a3fd91eef5f5fdeb805"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/fc5a92df083adf2fc30e45b3334f1a43a939d4a9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/fc5a92df083adf2fc30e45b3334f1a43a939d4a9","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKGZjNWE5MmRmMDgzYWRmMmZjMzBlNDViMzMzNGYxYTQzYTkzOWQ0YTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/45e9428af5b5bd5d477f0526538616de337a3fa7","sha":"45e9428af5b5bd5d477f0526538616de337a3fa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/45e9428af5b5bd5d477f0526538616de337a3fa7"}],"sha":"fc5a92df083adf2fc30e45b3334f1a43a939d4a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/fc5a92df083adf2fc30e45b3334f1a43a939d4a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/45e9428af5b5bd5d477f0526538616de337a3fa7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T06:32:26Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T06:32:26Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Fix two bugs the release run exposed: skipped publishes and a non-idempotent deprecate\n\nBoth publish steps were skipped on a run where one package was genuinely\nunpublished, and the run stayed green until a later step failed.\n\nThe cause was deriving GitHub Actions output names from package names:\n\n  key=$(echo \"$w\" | tr -c ''a-zA-Z0-9'' ''_'')\n\n`tr -c` converts everything outside the set, echo''s trailing newline included,\nso the outputs were written as `publish_cytoscape_web_app_runtime_` and\n`publishcreate_cytoscape_app_` while the `if:` conditions read the names without\nthose artefacts. An undefined output compares false, so both steps skipped —\nquietly, because a skipped step is not a failed one. Reproduced locally rather\nthan reasoned about, then replaced with two literals and a small function taking\nthe output name as an argument. Two literals cannot drift from two literals.\n\nThe deprecate step then failed with a 422 re-applying a notice that was already\nthere. It now reads the current value and only calls npm when the message would\nactually change, so a resumed run does not fail on a version that is already\ncorrect.\n\nVerified against the real registry before pushing this time: the decision logic\nnow yields runtime=false, scaffolder=true, which is the actual state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"34cc69ed14903ffeaa23f437089b3b1fbb5b2b20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/34cc69ed14903ffeaa23f437089b3b1fbb5b2b20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/45e9428af5b5bd5d477f0526538616de337a3fa7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/45e9428af5b5bd5d477f0526538616de337a3fa7","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDQ1ZTk0MjhhZjViNWJkNWQ0NzdmMDUyNjUzODYxNmRlMzM3YTNmYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/e44b73b9ef12ac28702318150aa064780bffdaee","sha":"e44b73b9ef12ac28702318150aa064780bffdaee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/e44b73b9ef12ac28702318150aa064780bffdaee"}],"sha":"45e9428af5b5bd5d477f0526538616de337a3fa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/45e9428af5b5bd5d477f0526538616de337a3fa7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/e44b73b9ef12ac28702318150aa064780bffdaee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T06:23:50Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T06:23:50Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Replace the impossible `latest` gate with a deprecation notice\n\nThe release gate as designed could not work, and 0.1.0 shipped before that was\ndiscovered.\n\nnpm assigns `latest` to a brand-new package''s first version whatever --tag says,\nand the registry REFUSES to delete it: DELETE .../dist-tags/latest returns 400\nafter a successful auth, a restriction the CLI documentation does not mention.\n@cytoscape-web/app-runtime@0.1.0 went out carrying both `next` and `latest`, and\nthe step meant to catch that was skipped because the run had already failed at\nthe second publish — a check that only runs on success is no check at all for\nthe runs that need it.\n\nHow the mistake was made is the reusable part, and the runbook records it: the\nreasoning verified that resolving a NONEXISTENT tag fails (npm view pkg@beta →\nE404) and then assumed the premise — that `latest` could be absent — without\ntesting it. Checking the conclusion is not checking the premise.\n\nThe gate is now a deprecation notice applied to every published version, and it\nis arguably the stronger mechanism. Almost nobody notices a missing dist-tag;\nnpm prints a deprecation on every install, to the person installing, at the\nmoment they do. The workflow applies it and then VERIFIES it, failing if a\npublished version carries none, and it runs whenever the release was not a dry\nrun — failed steps included, because a version published by a half-failed run is\nexactly the one that needs the notice.\n\n--tag next still buys something real, so the input gate stays with corrected\nreasoning: publishing with it leaves `latest` pointing where it already pointed,\nso a later Preview cannot become the default install by accident. Dispatching\nwith tag=latest is the one way to move it.\n\nTwo other fixes the failed runs exposed. `--access public` is required on the\nunscoped package too — npm refuses to generate provenance for a new package\nwithout it, whatever the scoping. And the workflow now skips a version already\non the registry, so a run that failed halfway can be resumed instead of dying on\na 403 for the package that already succeeded.\n\nCorrected everywhere the old claim appeared: design §3, the checklist, runbook\n§2 and §6-§8, both package READMEs and the roadmap''s Theme G row. The READMEs\nhad been telling people to type `npm create cytoscape-app@next` on the grounds\nthat the bare form would 404. It will not; that instruction was wrong.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"651586602611b0d256b8b1d167bec3bf3d15355c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/651586602611b0d256b8b1d167bec3bf3d15355c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/e44b73b9ef12ac28702318150aa064780bffdaee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/e44b73b9ef12ac28702318150aa064780bffdaee","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKGU0NGI3M2I5ZWYxMmFjMjg3MDIzMTgxNTBhYTA2NDc4MGJmZmRhZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/99b3cba059a0f23e2c1e71f42b80464dea10ce5b","sha":"99b3cba059a0f23e2c1e71f42b80464dea10ce5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/99b3cba059a0f23e2c1e71f42b80464dea10ce5b"}],"sha":"e44b73b9ef12ac28702318150aa064780bffdaee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/e44b73b9ef12ac28702318150aa064780bffdaee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/99b3cba059a0f23e2c1e71f42b80464dea10ce5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:24:31Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:24:31Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Add the repository field provenance validates, and check it before uploading\n\nThe 0.1.0 release failed at the registry:\n\n  npm error 422 Unprocessable Entity\n  Error verifying sigstore provenance bundle: Failed to validate repository\n  information: package.json: \"repository.url\" is \"\", expected to match\n  \"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples\" from provenance\n\nNeither package declared `repository`, and provenance requires it to match the\nrepository the sigstore bundle attests to. Both now declare it, with the\n`directory` field the monorepo case wants, plus homepage and bugs while we are\nin there. Nothing was published — the first publish failed and the second step\nwas skipped.\n\nThe interesting part is why nothing caught it. Provenance is validated by the\nREGISTRY, and `npm publish --dry-run` never contacts the registry, so it never\nruns that validation. This passed the local pre-flight, passed both publish\ndry runs, and still failed — after a human approval had been spent on it. A\ngreen dry run is not a green publish, and the runbook now says so where the dry\nrun is described.\n\nThe workflow now checks the field itself, before uploading anything, comparing\neach package against github.repository so the check cannot drift from the repo\nit runs in. It costs a second and fails without consuming an approval.\n\nRuled out along the way: the boolean input coerced correctly — the run really\ndid attempt a publish rather than silently dry-running again — and the token\nauthenticated, since a 422 means the request reached provenance validation\nrather than being rejected at the door. The unscoped package''s permissions are\nstill untested; it was skipped when the first publish failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c385ea7d8d8bbfd81c00b9ca5465217a20aad6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/4c385ea7d8d8bbfd81c00b9ca5465217a20aad6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/99b3cba059a0f23e2c1e71f42b80464dea10ce5b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/99b3cba059a0f23e2c1e71f42b80464dea10ce5b","node_id":"C_kwDOMaT2ftoAKDk5YjNjYmEwNTlhMGYyM2UyYzFlNzFmNDJiODA0NjRkZWExMGNlNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commit/bdf97458c6d584d511ce0440a134b939614db634","sha":"bdf97458c6d584d511ce0440a134b939614db634","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/bdf97458c6d584d511ce0440a134b939614db634"}],"sha":"99b3cba059a0f23e2c1e71f42b80464dea10ce5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/99b3cba059a0f23e2c1e71f42b80464dea10ce5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/commits/bdf97458c6d584d511ce0440a134b939614db634/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T01:37:15Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T01:37:15Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Spell out the bootstrap token''s settings, field by field\n\nSix fields, two of which fail in ways that do not point at themselves.\n\nAn IP allowlist looks like prudent hardening and breaks the publish outright:\nGitHub-hosted runners have dynamic egress IPs, and the resulting error does not\nname the field. Bypass 2FA has to be ENABLED — without it npm asks for an OTP\nand there is nobody at the keyboard, which is the whole reason a token exists in\nCI at all. Organizations is No access on npm''s own authority: its documentation\nsays that permission \"does not give the token the right to publish packages\nmanaged by the organization\", so granting it adds reach without adding ability.\n\nOne field npm does not document, and it is the one that matters here: whether\nselecting a SCOPE permits publishing a package that does not yet exist in it.\nBoth of ours are new, and create-cytoscape-app is unscoped besides, so it cannot\nbe picked from a list of packages that do not exist.\n\nThe runbook says to start narrow anyway. A refusal costs one failed job and\npublishes nothing — a 403 is a clean failure — whereas starting at All Packages\ngrants more than needed and leaves nobody able to say whether it was necessary.\n\nAn alternative is recorded and argued against rather than left unsaid: publishing\ncreate-cytoscape-app by hand once, purely to create the name, so a scope-limited\ntoken covers the rest. That trades a broad token living for minutes against a\nmanual, unattested release. The token is the smaller exposure, and unlike the\nrelease it can be deleted.\n\nStep 3 now says to delete in all three places — npm account, environment secret,\nworkflow lines. A revoked token still sitting in a secret store is confusing\nlater; a live one nobody references is worse.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7154f7d98639b499655b816e159ed61886ff2d48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/trees/7154f7d98639b499655b816e159ed61886ff2d48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web-app-examples/git/commits/bdf97458c6d584d511ce0440a134b939614db634","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use