"https://api.github.com/users/farhan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/ced1bf4183d13bb92124ec6ba3dba62f46026586/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:05:47Z","email":"farhan.khan@arbisoft.com","name":"Muhammad Farhan Khan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:05:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: run CI once per push to master to avoid coverage race (#293)\n\n* fix: run CI once per push to master to avoid coverage race\n\nrelease.yml calls ci.yml via workflow_call on every push to master,\nso the separate push: trigger in ci.yml fired CI twice concurrently.\nBoth runs raced to upload to the Codecov coverage data branch.\n\nRemove the push: trigger from ci.yml; release.yml''s workflow_call\ncovers pushes to master already.\n\nAlso replace the \"Version bumped\" PR template checklist item with a\nConventional Commits reminder — versioning is now automated by\npython-semantic-release and the manual checkbox is misleading.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org>","tree":{"sha":"841eb00592e0580052337ef322e154f60e69865f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/trees/841eb00592e0580052337ef322e154f60e69865f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/commits/ced1bf4183d13bb92124ec6ba3dba62f46026586","verification":{"payload":"tree 841eb00592e0580052337ef322e154f60e69865f\nparent b098f8072899c5c0c5885e1b2fc6f2a9444dbcbf\nauthor Muhammad Farhan Khan <farhan.khan@arbisoft.com> 1791381947 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791381947 -0400\n\nfix: run CI once per push to master to avoid coverage race (#293)\n\n* fix: run CI once per push to master to avoid coverage race\n\nrelease.yml calls ci.yml via workflow_call on every push to master,\nso the separate push: trigger in ci.yml fired CI twice concurrently.\nBoth runs raced to upload to the Codecov coverage data branch.\n\nRemove the push: trigger from ci.yml; release.yml''s workflow_call\ncovers pushes to master already.\n\nAlso replace the \"Version bumped\" PR template checklist item with a\nConventional Commits reminder — versioning is now automated by\npython-semantic-release and the manual checkbox is misleading.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxlG7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsyUQAEiW87kPsZcqLl2dJccpzxD0\nzrXJ2VhB5zIdCXkecfcZoy09LA782m9vmcOgM1Mhq1WKClKGrQDFQ6ed5CBBoFJ0\noeJQayQBRsAdKTKX2MyER8mGylh0q1fg4maTgOkeRmwNCyAbHV7vgPutmT+qjFLz\nZ4sKoQKdn6h7Il3NOLwpI8t1g/rnDfU7ZsdeY+vq1CXtFhUczsVg9TM+JeQg/CYz\nuSbsmbY0fXmzGatzBr6VjeonB9ySaY+8Wr1/nYoAwqW5wamGeyZSRBBJBPCPnPw5\nZiHtc3YFemhfXDmQwQ7MDsxgQa7MTiubQd7EyPfnGQ2J2azj85v9f3dkXq0UEt7D\nBi8blyrwWy8P8Ur4BihY+ihsXvxLj/8VGdOpCvwQCbInn737v++o/U1d+o2GvFAC\n0r5m0ZBeTBWx0Umwk2h9ooOE1rYnUcRUQX4pFjA3sd8GHDCXuIdNMRzEVlq2f1fI\nj5rJLfv+8PhHP/2hn3ThItzzVxifUth64w6iER0W14gkBpS4g8sM/tdT3hXxYtUp\nG4MS/qybi5YnOnYq4VR7iYdSfLUxWunwFniqy4knZ+cpPfrOggZ+53wRxSxcMWHn\nUIUDyI7i7YeCdGhfdzU05TaxYFVQED+OqgUGmInbhPD9OkExQiTGa24lTyZzDBq5\nlLG6o4JEedJ34S0I8bUt\n=Bod7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T14:05:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/ced1bf4183d13bb92124ec6ba3dba62f46026586","node_id":"C_kwDOMa6u_9oAKGNlZDFiZjQxODNkMTNiYjkyMTI0ZWM2YmEzZGJhNjJmNDYwMjY1ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/b098f8072899c5c0c5885e1b2fc6f2a9444dbcbf","sha":"b098f8072899c5c0c5885e1b2fc6f2a9444dbcbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/b098f8072899c5c0c5885e1b2fc6f2a9444dbcbf"}],"sha":"ced1bf4183d13bb92124ec6ba3dba62f46026586","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/ced1bf4183d13bb92124ec6ba3dba62f46026586"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26253150?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhtishamShahid","id":26253150,"login":"AhtishamShahid","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MjUzMTUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/b098f8072899c5c0c5885e1b2fc6f2a9444dbcbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:39:03Z","email":"ahtisham300@gmail.com","name":"Ahtisham Shahid"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:39:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: report endorsed status for threads in MySQL thread lists (#292)\n\nMySQLBackend.get_endorsed() returns a dict keyed by the thread id as a\nstring, but threads_presentor() looked it up with the integer primary\nkey, so every thread in a list was reported as unendorsed. Answered\nquestions therefore lost their \"answered\" state in the discussions\nsidebar after a page reload, while the single-thread endpoint (which\ndoes not go through threads_presentor) kept reporting them correctly.\n\nLook the thread up by str(thread.pk), matching the read state and abuse\nflag lookups next to it.","tree":{"sha":"c974f3020de1fb2696ceb5aa3fb4c3ebc96e9a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/trees/c974f3020de1fb2696ceb5aa3fb4c3ebc96e9a9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/commits/b098f8072899c5c0c5885e1b2fc6f2a9444dbcbf","verification":{"payload":"tree c974f3020de1fb2696ceb5aa3fb4c3ebc96e9a9e\nparent d3955539039ab2874f436eecc85475b54936db08\nauthor Ahtisham Shahid <ahtisham300@gmail.com> 1790771943 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790771943 +0500\n\nfix: report endorsed status for threads in MySQL thread lists (#292)\n\nMySQLBackend.get_endorsed() returns a dict keyed by the thread id as a\nstring, but threads_presentor() looked it up with the integer primary\nkey, so every thread in a list was reported as unendorsed. Answered\nquestions therefore lost their \"answered\" state in the discussions\nsidebar after a page reload, while the single-thread endpoint (which