flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/d3955539039ab2874f436eecc85475b54936db08","node_id":"C_kwDOMa6u_9oAKGQzOTU1NTM5MDM5YWIyODc0ZjQzNmVlY2M4NTQ3NWI1NDkzNmRiMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/1072456743a090984d0cc338620832e2389420b2","sha":"1072456743a090984d0cc338620832e2389420b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/1072456743a090984d0cc338620832e2389420b2"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/6a4135f7aa5599f973a3fa830478f41ee68a04d7","sha":"6a4135f7aa5599f973a3fa830478f41ee68a04d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/6a4135f7aa5599f973a3fa830478f41ee68a04d7"}],"sha":"d3955539039ab2874f436eecc85475b54936db08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/d3955539039ab2874f436eecc85475b54936db08"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/1072456743a090984d0cc338620832e2389420b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T06:31:12Z","email":"tmacey@boundlessnotions.com","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T06:31:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: make the Typesense search backend usable (#289)\n\nEvery forum search on the Typesense backend fails against a real server.\nTwo independent defects, both present since the backend shipped in #225:\n\n`build_search_parameters()` passes `per_page=FORUM_MAX_DEEP_SEARCH_COMMENT_COUNT`\n(1000). Typesense caps `per_page` at 250 and rejects anything higher with\nHTTP 422, so this fires on every search, filtered or not. The constant is\nshared with the Elasticsearch backend, which passes it as `size` under a\n`max_result_window` of 10000, and with Meilisearch, which passes it as `limit`\nunder a `maxTotalHits` of 1000 -- only Typesense caps low enough to break.\nRather than lower the deep-search budget for this backend alone, walk pages of\n250 until the budget is covered or a short page says the results are exhausted.\nSearches returning fewer than 250 hits, which is nearly all of them, still cost\none request.\n\n`collection_schema()` declares `commentable_id`; `build_search_parameters()`\nfiltered on `commentable_ids`, so scoping a search to discussion topics failed\nwith HTTP 400 \"Could not find a filter field\". Corrected to the singular field\nname the collection actually declares -- no reindex needed.\n\nNeither defect was reachable from the existing tests, which mock the Typesense\nclient and so cannot observe a rejection from the server. Add a Typesense\nservice to the e2e compose file and cover both against it; three of the four\nnew tests fail on the current code with the errors above.\n\n`TYPESENSE_URLS` in the test settings pointed at 0.0.0.0:8108, where nothing\nruns; it now points at the e2e container, mapped to 5108 to match the ports\nElasticsearch and Meilisearch already use there.","tree":{"sha":"323e4a21a3d96f5bac6a08e389c7e60bba7b9ca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/trees/323e4a21a3d96f5bac6a08e389c7e60bba7b9ca9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/commits/1072456743a090984d0cc338620832e2389420b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 323e4a21a3d96f5bac6a08e389c7e60bba7b9ca9\nparent d5b08e757c93a34c0fd4e274cde7f2ad0b4d7394\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@boundlessnotions.com> 1788849072 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788849072 +0500\n\nfix: make the Typesense search backend usable (#289)\n\nEvery forum search on the Typesense backend fails against a real server.\nTwo independent defects, both present since the backend shipped in #225:\n\n`build_search_parameters()` passes `per_page=FORUM_MAX_DEEP_SEARCH_COMMENT_COUNT`\n(1000). Typesense caps `per_page` at 250 and rejects anything higher with\nHTTP 422, so this fires on every search, filtered or not. The constant is\nshared with the Elasticsearch backend, which passes it as `size` under a\n`max_result_window` of 10000, and with Meilisearch, which passes it as `limit`\nunder a `maxTotalHits` of 1000 -- only Typesense caps low enough to break.\nRather than lower the deep-search budget for this backend alone, walk pages of\n250 until the budget is covered or a short page says the results are exhausted.\nSearches returning fewer than 250 hits, which is nearly all of them, still cost\none request.\n\n`collection_schema()` declares `commentable_id`; `build_search_parameters()`\nfiltered on `commentable_ids`, so scoping a search to discussion topics failed\nwith HTTP 400 \"Could not find a filter field\". Corrected to the singular field\nname the collection actually declares -- no reindex needed.\n\nNeither defect was reachable from the existing tests, which mock the Typesense\nclient and so cannot observe a rejection from the server. Add a Typesense\nservice to the e2e compose file and cover both against it; three of the four\nnew tests fail on the current code with the errors above.\n\n`TYPESENSE_URLS` in the test settings pointed at 0.0.0.0:8108, where nothing\nruns; it now points at the e2e container, mapped to 5108 to match the ports\nElasticsearch and Meilisearch already use there.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn6uwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAez4QAGh+tcIhRTUT7ofd22cjPKVE\nMSmUtekOJXcUtUiNxzPYp2mNqsjs42K31Bhqq1wpv8WK95VRmKCAoWdUmGRmeqT+\nDTSbxfchtYVYI0waS1Ag4vlccUN6hqAHD7ehzkWvBQh0ou3d7PXLeiePxOEmmBJ3\nBYTtFYCqJCbAdjf7EguiphCpEVRgUwM99Wr+IPcpDQFHflAcsj18g5jDFjSO/4dC\nv+v5fyjDqI8EMeSV0HE60ht4N7qZGIxLHJpYfMNjcZRVFGa0Yuu5lzIKyyfVPuFm\naBI66MVeRWCAIuIplvPd4U2rEGQ8kkbbK8xPGf8w8u8ivM2/WzW4XchpYcCs/P81\nJ9OuiYEXC1w1tzNusvaB7vcX1731LfXeK8lRV1E58TUQNBTFSp0BzkeSQB94x1Po\nZrR/kmmxT/Nf8WEtHq8YREIMa/KhGQcwgqE8Br8U99/+d3ifL6LRG7asuYTVzq1Z\npBzzMGDpepfY1s+0emab0OY53vYMPwxg+TtvYdsv8jAUpSvYO3T85P8J9TutGCF0\n9eRsdnIQQnM11tRQdEDSVju91zIG+ivia5/az8qrzQiaN3sHooN5+B7sxV2lO/Dr\nHhPR8xjOB4C4XeiwTdPJsiqxKnB9Z7XeX88+Tid5E+PhqvHr39Tl2+Kkdd7nrJC6\nZCTdSI4VVj7nRE2qYkns\n=+4EU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T06:31:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/1072456743a090984d0cc338620832e2389420b2","node_id":"C_kwDOMa6u_9oAKDEwNzI0NTY3NDNhMDkwOTg0ZDBjYzMzODYyMDgzMmUyMzg5NDIwYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/d5b08e757c93a34c0fd4e274cde7f2ad0b4d7394","sha":"d5b08e757c93a34c0fd4e274cde7f2ad0b4d7394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/d5b08e757c93a34c0fd4e274cde7f2ad0b4d7394"}],"sha":"1072456743a090984d0cc338620832e2389420b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/1072456743a090984d0cc338620832e2389420b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3189670?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Agrendalath","id":3189670,"login":"Agrendalath","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODk2NzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Agrendalath","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/d5b08e757c93a34c0fd4e274cde7f2ad0b4d7394/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T06:29:14Z","email":"piotr@surowiec.it","name":"Piotr Surowiec"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T06:29:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: do not update LMS user during retirement (#239)\n\n* fix: do not update LMS user during retirement\n\n1. Modifying users is already handled by the LMS retirement pipeline.\nThe `forum` library should not alter LMS users during retirement.\n2. Changing the email to an empty string results in integrity errors\nin the MySQL backend, because the email must be unique.\n\n* fix: ignore non-existent users during retirement\n\nIf the user does not exist in the forum backend, there is nothing to retire.\n\n* test: improve coverage\n\nThe previous two commits indirectly increased\nthe number of lines missed by unit tests.","tree":{"sha":"81d46d0f9d1cbcb518c852e24578e5455d57248d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/trees/81d46d0f9d1cbcb518c852e24578e5455d57248d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/commits/d5b08e757c93a34c0fd4e274cde7f2ad0b4d7394","verification":{"payload":"tree 81d46d0f9d1cbcb518c852e24578e5455d57248d\nparent 2f56d6226011e7eb319e4ab6b9f5c2a75bfb7d5f\nauthor Piotr Surowiec <piotr@surowiec.it> 1788848954 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788848954 +0500\n\nfix: do not update LMS user during retirement (#239)\n\n* fix: do not update LMS user during retirement\n\n1. Modifying users is already handled by the LMS retirement pipeline.\nThe `forum` library should not alter LMS users during retirement.\n2. Changing the email to an empty string results in integrity errors\nin the MySQL backend, because the email must be unique.\n\n* fix: ignore non-existent users during retirement\n\nIf the user does not exist in the forum backend, there is nothing to retire.\n\n* test: improve coverage\n\nThe previous two commits indirectly increased\nthe number of lines missed by unit tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn6s6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATcQQAEKhcm4d1gcW8TEoP21HeyxQ\nCG8zH2V+8sM2qPVhMu/4M3QpIW0YYwnTJh8UmtrMpRIxorJ8bqLRm304xLL6hVT1\nAZVsyJ/6uQe9ETP9/daPComeo7EuE/1gdJinJg1BXI9CHEwrJKHNIjs4fQracw15\ned/dUyrSmav78ZVvswv+8dryQqOyVOkwE9JPqNRQZYPfe47q3nUG5RhD7ELtCZ0S\nKCi+FEnzXt0PwOGqfIrNXX8pcF9mDxc02MqOIgm8ETKTcVW59RJcooWgnRDB8wPl\nLjOasyvqY7Jn5S51CjaEq8JqZVzq+SQ2r5my541gVuK5XQFeBXxRRbtUtjLjKtvc\nwXvJhoCqrd8euLZ7bQaraX4Q75c+YR5N44MGA0iaZ0/I3q6xBzM7izr3nGX4l5MS\n5Nf1G6gfsgy4e+n7R9+apy+oHb5/DzoAS67jWOcapZ2IoHaeSio4awNbLFdZ+MHc\nBIAkV9gwNDWpFu5OBUqlgqPYJBrm7J7uMx2jJcuzudGYuQUBIeNEdGekoK12gCEl\nYK+ukrNdhXqL61QciVdo1MMaJxb5N/UocG7nqVjO0CB/3kDTDjS4encUanzJSRqF\nZfRoZvfIIZoalObKRQ7diMOYTr3zsgDzVRE9CTi4RziENuW+U1cx0mvFlShTxR9g\nZSlaQ34feUWQ4OSNMcpE\n=mPj6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T06:29:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/d5b08e757c93a34c0fd4e274cde7f2ad0b4d7394","node_id":"C_kwDOMa6u_9oAKGQ1YjA4ZTc1N2M5M2EzNGMwZmQ0ZTI3NGNkZTdmMmFkMGI0ZDczOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/2f56d6226011e7eb319e4ab6b9f5c2a75bfb7d5f","sha":"2f56d6226011e7eb319e4ab6b9f5c2a75bfb7d5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/2f56d6226011e7eb319e4ab6b9f5c2a75bfb7d5f"}],"sha":"d5b08e757c93a34c0fd4e274cde7f2ad0b4d7394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/d5b08e757c93a34c0fd4e274cde7f2ad0b4d7394"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25842457?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farhan","id":25842457,"login":"farhan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1ODQyNDU3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/6a4135f7aa5599f973a3fa830478f41ee68a04d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T15:10:51Z","email":"farhan.khan@arbisoft.com","name":"farhan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T15:10:51Z","email":"farhan.khan@arbisoft.com","name":"farhan"},"message":"fix: make release workflow compatible with immutable releases\n\nThe org has immutable releases enabled, which freezes a release''s assets\nthe moment it is published. The old flow let python-semantic-release\npublish the GitHub Release and then attached the built distributions\nafterwards via publish-action, which now fails with HTTP 422 (\"cannot\nupload assets to an immutable release\"). That failure aborts the release\njob before publish_to_pypi runs, so the tag is created but the package is\nnever shipped.\n\nAdopt the sample-plugin immutable-safe pattern: set vcs_release=\"false\"\nso python-semantic-release commits, tags, and builds but does not publish\nthe release, then create it with `gh release create` which uploads the\nassets to a draft and publishes it atomically -- the ordering immutable\nreleases require. All actions are SHA-pinned to their latest releases\nwith matching version comments (checkout v7.0.1, upload-artifact v7.0.1,\ndownload-artifact v8.0.1, python-semantic-release v10.6.2,\ngh-action-pypi-publish v1.14.2). PyPI keeps OIDC trusted publishing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d27d33a308b9880391f31816f6c63007ebf12500","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/trees/d27d33a308b9880391f31816f6c63007ebf12500"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/commits/6a4135f7aa5599f973a3fa830478f41ee68a04d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25842457?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farhan","id":25842457,"login":"farhan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1ODQyNDU3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farhan/received_event