7d0f6c04223a08763e916","sha":"2b84d1a0a2a48e155757d0f6c04223a08763e916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/2b84d1a0a2a48e155757d0f6c04223a08763e916"}],"sha":"78b36e42365ae2758c92d794a53759e6316bc7a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/78b36e42365ae2758c92d794a53759e6316bc7a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9714796?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelallan72","id":9714796,"login":"samuelallan72","node_id":"U_kgDOAJQ8bA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelallan72","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/2b84d1a0a2a48e155757d0f6c04223a08763e916/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-27T19:17:19Z","email":"samuel@opencraft.com","name":"Samuel Allan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-27T19:17:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add Typesense backend for search (#225)\n\nSupport searching forum threads and comments using Typesense as\na backend.\n\nThis is completely backwards compatible; Meilisearch can\nstill be used as the backend with no changes, and existing installations\nwill continue to be configured to use Meilisearch.\n\nThe new backend can be enabled by setting:\n\n```py\nTYPESENSE_ENABLED = True\n```\n\nYou can also manually set the backend for testing with something like:\n\n```py\nFORUM_SEARCH_BACKEND = \"forum.search.typesense.TypesenseBackend\"\n```\n\nConfiguring the Typesense backend can be done with these settings:\n\n```py\nTYPESENSE_API_KEY = \"your-secret-api-key\"\nTYPESENSE_URLS = [\"https://typesense-1.example.com:8108\", \"https://typesense-2.example.com:8108\"]\n```\n\nThe actual implementation differs from the Meilisearch backend\nin some areas, mostly for internal efficiency.\nFor example, a single index is used to cover both threads and comments,\nwhile Meilisearch uses two.\nIt aims to produce comparable results for searches by end users though.\n\nDocs about this are being added to Open edX Documentation\nin https://github.com/openedx/docs.openedx.org/pull/1376 ,\nso that will be the source of truth.\n\nPrivate-ref: https://tasks.opencraft.com/browse/BB-9975","tree":{"sha":"5d5f51f9136dcbc3eb0a480964cecc22f9ada03d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/trees/5d5f51f9136dcbc3eb0a480964cecc22f9ada03d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/commits/2b84d1a0a2a48e155757d0f6c04223a08763e916","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d5f51f9136dcbc3eb0a480964cecc22f9ada03d\nparent a5f31e680cbb9b1e4b4f4f83f177b03563198f91\nauthor Samuel Allan <samuel@opencraft.com> 1769541439 +1030\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1769541439 +0500\n\nfeat: add Typesense backend for search (#225)\n\nSupport searching forum threads and comments using Typesense as\na backend.\n\nThis is completely backwards compatible; Meilisearch can\nstill be used as the backend with no changes, and existing installations\nwill continue to be configured to use Meilisearch.\n\nThe new backend can be enabled by setting:\n\n```py\nTYPESENSE_ENABLED = True\n```\n\nYou can also manually set the backend for testing with something like:\n\n```py\nFORUM_SEARCH_BACKEND = \"forum.search.typesense.TypesenseBackend\"\n```\n\nConfiguring the Typesense backend can be done with these settings:\n\n```py\nTYPESENSE_API_KEY = \"your-secret-api-key\"\nTYPESENSE_URLS = [\"https://typesense-1.example.com:8108\", \"https://typesense-2.example.com:8108\"]\n```\n\nThe actual implementation differs from the Meilisearch backend\nin some areas, mostly for internal efficiency.\nFor example, a single index is used to cover both threads and comments,\nwhile Meilisearch uses two.\nIt aims to produce comparable results for searches by end users though.\n\nDocs about this are being added to Open edX Documentation\nin https://github.com/openedx/docs.openedx.org/pull/1376 ,\nso that will be the source of truth.\n\nPrivate-ref: https://tasks.opencraft.com/browse/BB-9975","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpeQ8/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaeMQAG2JPwVzDMwqGB/tQ4Qc9olx\n+b97dDFM7nlT4sbP6Jvx9E9D1rl/KmrnFcPwHttPGk5KaWiVEquym+7a5oRhnU97\nZ8YyKTYtsIqrsbLlt8ZVi7jmtAAZGAO1v/B1qhGox7E19iOyUcTUhP30BbxsC/Ad\nVl33AgSmVmoA4v2cYBSSR+0TQl/DQ6cfUcNqnzs0kzrC3StCgGXi0JZPU1Bnt9Eq\nBv/tLCFopdPwmJ3MVmAy2142hiH8NAtLpOClNG0/iLcUni+VC9HYauJCKvV2tAkM\nNnuyO4kYCUhX3v1SdOo+6jdy+IphXKn91B+eyOF7YeEXa6o5L/VhZTfNHrJEOU9g\nVuoCJrI4g9hPnM8inQRgxb7E2CAmIlbc5fqH+wevHxjrYdrSxgcxOpcybRyin4D4\nb0e25HD0hsi8nKqzxJAJESxvcah1t5XcNOhj5AfgSRgk2HHWAD1olnY1o5LhzEHq\nq0efgWzDwFR1srt0U0S3npdTWmHZhHs9rzvD+EcHYIRvvWHgYsXaSgS4aE0zO/Du\nwwlqtSPC+yjcLMrCs83bcnmFZkl7sAOAbGSfVvRuZHxa9bVwitai9BJkUPmJTZvL\n4gxek8Fav4pHSiY2kQ5yEQ87vvPBSzWLuN+VCAQgF2o3fOTztvNmuJCQIB7STT4I\n/5mrDYGrDCvxKwrAOr35\n=kL1W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-01-27T19:17:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/2b84d1a0a2a48e155757d0f6c04223a08763e916","node_id":"C_kwDOMa6u_9oAKDJiODRkMWEwYTJhNDhlMTU1NzU3ZDBmNmMwNDIyM2EwODc2M2U5MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/forum/commit/a5f31e680cbb9b1e4b4f4f83f177b03563198f91","sha":"a5f31e680cbb9b1e4b4f4f83f177b03563198f91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/a5f31e680cbb9b1e4b4f4f83f177b03563198f91"}],"sha":"2b84d1a0a2a48e155757d0f6c04223a08763e916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/2b84d1a0a2a48e155757d0f6c04223a08763e916"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68893403?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/taimoor-ahmed-1","id":68893403,"login":"taimoor-ahmed-1","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODkzNDAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taimoor-ahmed-1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/a5f31e680cbb9b1e4b4f4f83f177b03563198f91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-08T05:33:36Z","email":"68893403+taimoor-ahmed-1@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Taimoor Ahmed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-08T05:33:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Optimize MySQL backend APIs to improve performance (#246)\n\nThis commit introduces query optimizations to reduce database queries and\nimprove response times:\n\n- Fixed N+1 queries in threads_presentor, get_paginated_user_stats, and\n  other methods using select_related/prefetch_related\n- Optimized get_read_states to prefetch data in bulk instead of individual\n  queries\n- Optimized get_abuse_flagged_count and get_endorsed with bulk aggregations\n- Removed duplicate annotations in handle_threads_query\n- Added query optimizations across prepare_thread, validate_thread_and_user,\n  and other methods\n\nPerformance impact: Reduced queries from O(n) to O(1)/O(k), eliminated N+1\npatterns, improved bulk operations. All changes maintain backward compatibility.\n\nCo-authored-by: Taimoor  Ahmed <taimoor.ahmed@A006-01711.local>","tree":{"sha":"360580cbf504b0e053189735c65aeecba8f27c71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/trees/360580cbf504b0e053189735c65aeecba8f27c71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/commits/a5f31e680cbb9b1e4b4f4f83f177b03563198f91","verification":{"payload":"tree 360580cbf504b0e053189735c65aeecba8f27c71\nparent 9955b4259143bccf1ca5d4f8c2a2476224e80ef6\nauthor Taimoor Ahmed <68893403+taimoor-ahmed-1@users.noreply.github.com> 1765172016 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1765172016 +0500\n\nfeat: Optimize MySQL backend APIs to improve performance (#246)\n\nThis commit introduces query optimizations to reduce database queries and\nimprove response times:\n\n- Fixed N+1 queries in threads_presentor, get_paginated_user_stats, and\n  other methods using select_related/prefetch_related\n- Optimized get_read_states to prefetch data in bulk instead of individual\n  queries\n- Optimized get_abuse_flagged_count and get_endorsed with bulk aggregations\n- Removed duplicate annotations in handle_threads_query\n- Added query optimizations across prepare_thread, validate_thread_and_user,\n  and other methods\n\nPerformance impact: Reduced queries from O(n) to O(1)/O(k), eliminated N+1\npatterns, improved bulk operations. All changes maintain backward compatibility.\n\nCo-authored-by: Taimoor  Ahmed <taimoor.ahmed@A006-01711.local>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpNmMwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMd8QAE7WuyLr6ju+MUW3yl4DFfBQ\ne8SLAMdjb48l2zxcIPxjnIoXmgdg92equIe1EiWHL9tlLvzutL9MZN92obinrIKt\nJYjrEq/vFof0YPVouLI5UX1EDBHdlhKTRV/g2/HWWJtUiyq4odhraehXFtCHFo72\nWYjnpf9pw2NyF0aEbLRYuthb395BctgZ9XsJlDkk0HFjB5MpPvcXRTqfIyrvclXA\nGezdxSya9ED5NtCvvKyGyu8iAqDQiCSqT/v+V0KD/esg+3XN/N8m4K8a/WRVfeig\nA1ALVl2T2kQBe2OErjkgipp5eUL08PYLVTTuN3r8V0ytmKNHaWJNRPEtJFzjZmNO\nueq/5xgbteG/jJwxzC+jKGL9OU/24scMtzI7DgcWxKbpGa0bFTVS1PyjNClJGhAn\nQBYtnFzd9bU+zvE9Q0d8L0S2XCIQSX7mszm1fRPBadb1zeMFzUa7IXtcS0O1jPVb\nU8iZEJc65qJRyrC9eOCEfiadxMH2pOMNzOGUn5kX5it25ZsptQmg6Thmg1D8T1l9\nUVq1rc2p8rBcytkD7oMP57/I9Ov9hDkzGp+0Icwdp7nWKMFh/kFSdfukc1ib1YVX\nrDD38EUQtOtZJZxCD7ZGgcCcdSPDR53ucZIMODp31s5EaQ6627cQiO/Biajm+Mlq\nSF4YZlMvVE6Y3aQ90FYK\n=qBUM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-12-08T05:33:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_us