gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/commits/810c2b0c49d4f7cbeaaf80c7627ecb462b3bbc94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-09T11:03:33Z","email":"tmacey@boundlessnotions.com","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-09T11:03:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Add author field to ContentSerializer for Forums V2 API compatibility (#245)\n\nThe Forums V2 API responses were missing the ''author'' attribute that is expected by\nthe frontend, causing issues when displaying comment/thread author information.\n\nAnalysis showed that:\n- The ContentSerializer already has ''username'' field mapped to ''author_username''\n- Frontend expects an ''author'' field in addition to ''username''\n- Both should reference the same source data (author_username)\n\nThis change adds the ''author'' field to the DRF serializer, mapped to the same\n''author_username'' source as ''username'', maintaining backward compatibility while\nfixing the missing field issue.\n\nFixes compatibility issues with Forums V2 API responses.","tree":{"sha":"5eecd069f9aa583cb0f8e872e3b00c81aca1e5bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/trees/5eecd069f9aa583cb0f8e872e3b00c81aca1e5bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/forum/git/commits/810c2b0c49d4f7cbeaaf80c7627ecb462b3bbc94","verification":{"payload":"tree 5eecd069f9aa583cb0f8e872e3b00c81aca1e5bb\nparent fb17be36eb36f0eae38df59ae194bcb83c12c415\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@boundlessnotions.com> 1762686213 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1762686213 +0500\n\nfix: Add author field to ContentSerializer for Forums V2 API compatibility (#245)\n\nThe Forums V2 API responses were missing the ''author'' attribute that is expected by\nthe frontend, causing issues when displaying comment/thread author information.\n\nAnalysis showed that:\n- The ContentSerializer already has ''username'' field mapped to ''author_username''\n- Frontend expects an ''author'' field in addition to ''username''\n- Both should reference the same source data (author_username)\n\nThis change adds the ''author'' field to the DRF serializer, mapped to the same\n''author_username'' source as ''username'', maintaining backward compatibility while\nfixing the missing field issue.\n\nFixes compatibility issues with Forums V2 API responses.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpEHUFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJaoQABMTPJHWkgofVCYiveYbbxVV\nEMy3mpZOW+z/8P8cEaVwsCHjXDhxi2o29oJ4JE/8wjWrfmOZhrpIvnRTMsSxkKcd\ngcj9+3iyYvfRslhhXSvqZRZhMSrnwP71yERIB2VYehHMlM8RxpLkcraEPPKyFOQY\nJgsC14ovHVH2wtaiDuOXQRh/XWeErqHP22/Q+G4OjVqbVqnNhh7YuRsYAHcMEUsi\nne+pqXkXhMy0VwC5V7LNYFRG1VJfx1brekxxuvwuj6B+32hhmILiRce9FZgSyM4t\nkDdewVGYEqart26QD/Q0v5Oy+0ZKkgjeK4E2oye2Hewj2kjeEpdpLy1f3GVLL3ev\nypoqKrcCMTlKqSJiVXwAfIOk0QvLUQUSJi0PnwdgNWLWWAHo35V0CBf92oC2ctXQ\nsUrB968FgpqLNqMaZT30O4uahImX2PslwUAg8QivuiK8MU9T6g6V7gVw6ncdP8go\nOrDjEgDyFpMx9LABAAxu7SrGzGpoavLxIPgFcnEwl/hG+S8ep+EPlanXu+D5A1YP\nON0BsFXEoFJOx8midJhwiIqi3wKRp6C574SHuv2d4SQHlrIu9nr0kAQgEG4dY4nm\nUyGxRZGTg3pmPWghFcYJmVsNE6kT7wf1G5xy7S0IvCRW9+8iCM7AJMKkYXpjeuxQ\naH88LLbDWDfxKzN/XTtN\n=v9Wg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-09T11:03:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.git