following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/cb5918e6fa918d3cf78dc843794d41f1c29df671/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T15:33:49Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T15:33:49Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"docs: ADR-0004 + PZEP-0003 — decouple Backoffice from IAM, scope IAM SDK Phase 1\n\nLive inventory of every cross-service call into IAM''s decision API found\nonly 6 call sites (onboarding 4, backoffice 1, partner 1, ~21 permission\nstrings) — a small, tractable surface for the open-source extraction\nalready planned in 11-iam-platform.md. Backoffice''s one call site was the\nonly one whose resource identifier depends on request-time GraphQL\ncontext rather than a static route, and its real permission model\n(migration 0002_create_iam_core.sql) turned out to be four roles with a\nstrictly nested static grant set — no dynamic policy features used.\n\nADR-0004 (Proposed): Backoffice stops calling IAM''s decision API — auth\nembeds active_tenant_role in the JWT (sourced from its own existing\niam_tenant_memberships_projection, no new cross-service call), Backoffice\nchecks a static compiled-in role->action table instead. No per-store ACL,\nno faster-than-refresh permission propagation — both explicitly accepted\ntradeoffs given neither is used today.\n\nPZEP-0003 (Draft): the combined implementation plan — Part 1 is the\nBackoffice decoupling above; Part 2 is a Go SDK (sdk/go, Authorize(ctx,\nprincipal, action, resource)) for IAM''s remaining real callers\n(onboarding, partner), replacing their hand-rolled gRPC client wrappers.\nBoth parts are independently shippable. No IAM wire contract change, no\nDB schema change.\n\nSRS-IAM-005 added to anchor the requirement; narrows but does not repeal\nSRS-IAM-001 (centralized policy stays IAM''s job for callers that actually\nneed dynamism — today that''s onboarding and IAM''s own admin console, not\nBackoffice).\n\nNothing implemented yet — proposal only, per this session''s brainstorming\nwith the user.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4ad27dc32819fb32d49bc8067ba3b44df12e4a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/e4ad27dc32819fb32d49bc8067ba3b44df12e4a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/cb5918e6fa918d3cf78dc843794d41f1c29df671","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/cb5918e6fa918d3cf78dc843794d41f1c29df671","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKGNiNTkxOGU2ZmE5MThkM2NmNzhkYzg0Mzc5NGQ0MWYxYzI5ZGY2NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/8968889af12f63b3eeac467d57ad608715ef7d8e","sha":"8968889af12f63b3eeac467d57ad608715ef7d8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/8968889af12f63b3eeac467d57ad608715ef7d8e"}],"sha":"cb5918e6fa918d3cf78dc843794d41f1c29df671","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/cb5918e6fa918d3cf78dc843794d41f1c29df671"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/8968889af12f63b3eeac467d57ad608715ef7d8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T15:05:51Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T15:05:51Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"fix(docker): switch dev frontend watchers to polling, fixes stale MFE rebuilds\n\nDocker Desktop''s WSL2 bind mounts don''t reliably forward inotify events\ninto the container, so vite build --watch (the 3 MFE remotes) and vite''s\ndev-server HMR watcher (the HOST) would silently stop reacting to host\nfile edits after some time — see the knowledge base entry for the\nincident this was found from (\"Module onboarding could not be loaded\").\n\nSet CHOKIDAR_USEPOLLING=true / CHOKIDAR_INTERVAL=300 on backoffice-remote,\niam-remote, onboarding-remote, and frontend in\ndeployments/docker/services.yml. Chokidar reads these env vars directly\nregardless of caller (Vite''s own watcher or Rollup''s --watch mode), so no\nvite.config changes needed.\n\nVerified live: edited a file, watched the container auto-rebuild within\nseconds via `docker logs -t`, with zero manual restart — both for the edit\nand for reverting it. Requires `docker compose up -d --build <service>`\n(recreate) to pick up, not just `docker restart`, for anyone already\nrunning a session from before this change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a0320649b38a012ae1c31466869ff5f4d535b2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/0a0320649b38a012ae1c31466869ff5f4d535b2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/8968889af12f63b3eeac467d57ad608715ef7d8e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/8968889af12f63b3eeac467d57ad608715ef7d8e","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKDg5Njg4ODlhZjEyZjYzYjNlZWFjNDY3ZDU3YWQ2MDg3MTVlZjdkOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/b1ac488a18723d23bd89a9a0d2ff07ad55d4619e","sha":"b1ac488a18723d23bd89a9a0d2ff07ad55d4619e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/b1ac488a18723d23bd89a9a0d2ff07ad55d4619e"}],"sha":"8968889af12f63b3eeac467d57ad608715ef7d8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/8968889af12f63b3eeac467d57ad608715ef7d8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/b1ac488a18723d23bd89a9a0d2ff07ad55d4619e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T15:00:51Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T15:00:51Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"docs: knowledge base entry for MFE remote watch going stale (Docker/WSL2)\n\nThe CollectionFilters overflow fix didn''t reach the browser after a\nrefresh — \"Module onboarding could not be loaded\". Root cause: all three\nMFE remote containers'' vite build --watch processes were alive but hadn''t\ndone a real rebuild in over 80 minutes despite repeated file edits — a\nDocker Desktop/WSL2 bind-mount inotify gap, not a code or network problem\n(remoteEntry.js was reachable throughout). Different root cause from the\n2026-07-11 port-forward incident despite the identical symptom.\n\nFix applied: docker restart on all three remote containers, forcing a\nfresh build. Documented the diagnostic signature (grep container logs for\n\"built in\" lines, a missing or suspiciously small rebuild after an edit is\nthe tell) since there''s no permanent fix identified this session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"152e9c77d5f1bcf0d39303c766d718b61fa21ae6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/152e9c77d5f1bcf0d39303c766d718b61fa21ae6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/b1ac488a18723d23bd89a9a0d2ff07ad55d4619e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/b1ac488a18723d23bd89a9a0d2ff07ad55d4619e","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKGIxYWM0ODhhMTg3MjNkMjNiZDg5YTlhMGQyZmYwN2FkNTVkNDYxOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/2abb18c4621269be3775e181c6aea6076caa20a8","sha":"2abb18c4621269be3775e181c6aea6076caa20a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/2abb18c4621269be3775e181c6aea6076caa20a8"}],"sha":"b1ac488a18723d23bd89a9a0d2ff07ad55d4619e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/b1ac488a18723d23bd89a9a0d2ff07ad55d4619e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/2abb18c4621269be3775e181c6aea6076caa20a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T14:45:36Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T14:45:36Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"fix(ui): stop CollectionFilters row overflowing narrow containers\n\nThe filter row (Filter field / Operator / Value / Add filter) used a CSS\nGrid with hard minmax minimums (10rem + 10rem + 12rem = 32rem) at the `md:`\nbreakpoint. That breakpoint checks viewport width, not the actual\ncontainer width — inside a narrower column (e.g. the left panel of\nonboarding''s Provisioning pipeline view, ~527px after padding), the grid\nstill enforced its minimums and overflowed, visually landing \"Add filter\"\non top of unrelated content in the neighboring panel.\n\nSwitch to flex-wrap with per-field min-width instead of a fixed-column\ngrid: fields grow to fill available space but wrap onto a new line when\nthe container is too narrow, instead of overflowing it. Fixes every\nconsumer of this shared component, not just the one screen it was\nreported on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6328ee706a43fbe091c31e6e01d1972d8bf47e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/c6328ee706a43fbe091c31e6e01d1972d8bf47e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/2abb18c4621269be3775e181c6aea6076caa20a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/2abb18c4621269be3775e181c6aea6076caa20a8","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKDJhYmIxOGM0NjIxMjY5YmUzNzc1ZTE4MWM2YWVhNjA3NmNhYTIwYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/40951150c22d3fa18b1d2c8716552132f9787f57","sha":"40951150c22d3fa18b1d2c8716552132f9787f57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/40951150c22d3fa18b1d2c8716552132f9787f57"}],"sha":"2abb18c4621269be3775e181c6aea6076caa20a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/2abb18c4621269be3775e181c6aea6076caa20a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/40951150c22d3fa18b1d2c8716552132f9787f57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T14:21:43Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T14:21:43Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"feat(shell): gate Provisioning/IAM sidebar links by platform vs org role\n\nSRS-IAM-003, unblocked after API-level backbone verification (explicit\nproduct decision, see backbone-flow-refactor.md). First slice: hide\nProvisioning and IAM from accounts that can''t use them, instead of showing\nevery link to every account regardless of role.\n\nAdd usePlatformAccess() (frontend/src/modules/shell/) — one\nlistOrganizations call already computes both signals server-side\n(internal/iam/controller/grpchandler/organization_methods.go:180-212):\ncanManagePlatform (real platform_owner/admin) and, for everyone else,\nwhether they belong to any organization at all. No new backend endpoint.\n\nNav rules: Home/Settings always shown; Provisioning only for\ncanManagePlatform; IAM shown for canManagePlatform OR membership in at\nleast one org, tagged ROOT or ORG respectively. While the resource is\nloading, both gated links stay hidden rather than flashing then\ndisappearing.\n\nVerified live against Docker dev: devowner@podzone.dev (real\nplatform_owner) gets canManagePlatform: true from the real endpoint. The\norg-only/no-org branches were verified by reading the server-side branch\nlogic, not exercised live (no JWT available this session for a plain\norganization_root or plain tenant-owner account).\n\nDoes not split /admin/iam into two consoles — same route, same console,\nwhich already adapts its own content via canManagePlatform. Does not add\na route guard for direct URL access — backend already 403s; this is nav\nvisibility (UX) only, not the security boundary (SRS-IAM-001).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"afe7e66457e98f2df9beb3e9a9537a5e5ebb682f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/afe7e66457e98f2df9beb3e9a9537a5e5ebb682f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/40951150c22d3fa18b1d2c8716552132f9787f57","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/40951150c22d3fa18b1d2c8716552132f9787f57","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKDQwOTUxMTUwYzIyZDNmYTE4YjFkMmM4NzE2NTUyMTMyZjk3ODdmNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/f9f94b71fcb5039cc6a90a36af4123c7920e06be","sha":"f9f94b71fcb5039cc6a90a36af4123c7920e06be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/f9f94b71fcb5039cc6a90a36af4123c7920e06be"}],"sha":"40951150c22d3fa18b1d2c8716552132f9787f57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/40951150c22d3fa18b1d2c8716552132f9787f57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/f9f94b71fcb5039cc6a90a36af4123c7920e06be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T14:14:15Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T14:14:15Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"docs: verify backbone flow end-to-end against live Docker dev (API level)\n\nUsed the dev-auth-bootstrap identity (devowner@podzone.dev, tenant-dev,\n\"Demo Store\") against the already-running full-profile stack: real JWT\nvalidation, onboarding''s request list, the readiness endpoint (confirms\nthe previous commit''s FE wiring gets exactly the response shape it\nexpects — ui_state: \"ready\" for the seeded ready request), and one\nprotected Backoffice GraphQL query (stores) succeeding for an authorized\nuser with a clean UNAUTHENTICATED error for no token.\n\nNot done this pass: browser-rendered UI screenshot (no headless-browser\ntool available in this environment) and the pending/provisioning/blocked/\nfailed ui_state branches (no seed data in those states). Recorded in\nbackbone-flow-refactor.md''s Exit Criteria per-line with what was and\nwasn''t confirmed, and in wire-store-readiness-frontend.md''s status.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0dafe5118e9b366e375ceec220eae376272edc45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/0dafe5118e9b366e375ceec220eae376272edc45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/f9f94b71fcb5039cc6a90a36af4123c7920e06be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/f9f94b71fcb5039cc6a90a36af4123c7920e06be","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKGY5Zjk0YjcxZmNiNTAzOWNjNmE5MGEzNmFmNDEyM2M3OTIwZTA2YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/2c6071d6b0365e6ad101024806e183850d5e35cb","sha":"2c6071d6b0365e6ad101024806e183850d5e35cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/2c6071d6b0365e6ad101024806e183850d5e35cb"}],"sha":"f9f94b71fcb5039cc6a90a36af4123c7920e06be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/f9f94b71fcb5039cc6a90a36af4123c7920e06be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/2c6071d6b0365e6ad101024806e183850d5e35cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T13:52:08Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T13:52:08Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"fix(onboarding): drive provisioning status badge from readiness endpoint\n\nProvisioningRequestsPanel derived its status badge color from a client-side\nprefix check on request.status (startsWith(''failed'') -> red). Per the\nreadiness contract''s mapping table this is wrong in two real cases:\nfailed_retryable should read as \"blocked\", not \"failed\"; and a request with\nstatus ''ready'' but placement/route not actually ready should also read as\n\"blocked\", not the green \"ready\" the old heuristic gave it.\n\nAdd getStoreReadiness to the onboarding service client and a small\ncreateStoreReadinessViewModel that fetches GET /requests/:id/readiness for\neach visible request; the badge now reads the backend''s authoritative\nui_state instead of re-deriving it. Backend endpoint was already\nimplemented and tested (docs/04-sprints/tasks/onboarding-readiness-api.md);\nthis was the missing FE half, tracked in\ndocs/06-recovery/backbone-flow-refactor.md gap #1.\n\nVerified via npm run build / build:onboarding / lint / format:check.\nNot yet verified end-to-end against a live backend in Docker dev.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5e2484eb23e8420078f99fa665a48e1da61e47b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/5e2484eb23e8420078f99fa665a48e1da61e47b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/2c6071d6b0365e6ad101024806e183850d5e35cb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/2c6071d6b0365e6ad101024806e183850d5e35cb","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKDJjNjA3MWQ2YjAzNjVlNmFkMTAxMDI0ODA2ZTE4Mzg1MGQ1ZTM1Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/cf459fb97e7ad2fc309584bf733edca3cf735d12","sha":"cf459fb97e7ad2fc309584bf733edca3cf735d12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/cf459fb97e7ad2fc309584bf733edca3cf735d12"}],"sha":"2c6071d6b0365e6ad101024806e183850d5e35cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/2c6071d6b0365e6ad101024806e183850d5e35cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/cf459fb97e7ad2fc309584bf733edca3cf735d12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T13:51:54Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T13:51:54Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"fix(frontend): collapse sidebar workspace switcher into one compact row\n\nThe workspace control was a label + full-width button (empty state) or\nlabel + info box + subtext + button (selected state) — up to 4 lines of\nvertical space for what is just a link to the store chooser. Replace both\nstates with one fixed-height (h-12) clickable row: chip/initials, store\nname + tenant id (or \"Choose a store\"), chevron. Pattern documented in\ndesign-system.md (see previous commit).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5684408ce659659ecdb7d38e004353527ec88e92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/5684408ce659659ecdb7d38e004353527ec88e92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/cf459fb97e7ad2fc309584bf733edca3cf735d12","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/cf459fb97e7ad2fc309584bf733edca3cf735d12","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKGNmNDU5ZmI5N2U3YWQyZmMzMDk1ODRiZjczM2VkY2EzY2Y3MzVkMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/4fd73f1960d9b88824ff6fad6ccc42e1a318d054","sha":"4fd73f1960d9b88824ff6fad6ccc42e1a318d054","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/4fd73f1960d9b88824ff6fad6ccc42e1a318d054"}],"sha":"cf459fb97e7ad2fc309584bf733edca3cf735d12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/cf459fb97e7ad2fc309584bf733edca3cf735d12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/4fd73f1960d9b88824ff6fad6ccc42e1a318d054/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T13:51:39Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T13:51:39Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"fix(frontend): relocate admin-settings from onboarding remote to shell\n\nadmin-settings/ (sessions, audit, invites, platform roles, team access)\nlived in the onboarding MFE but every panel called @podzone/shared/services/\n{auth,iam} — none called onboarding''s backend. It briefly moved through the\niam remote first, but landed in the shell instead: apps/iam is the FE\nsurface most likely to be reused if IAM ships as a standalone product (see\n11-iam-platform.md''s extraction plan), and this page is Podzone-product\ncomposition (workspace/store copy, GW_API_URL labeled \"Store GraphQL API\"),\nnot generic IAM UI.\n\n/admin/settings keeps its URL; ownership moves from a federation-loaded\nremote page to a shell-local lazyRouteComponent (no network fetch needed\nsince it''s already bundled into the host). onboarding/vite.config.ts drops\nthe now-unused expose, federation.d.ts drops the ambient module decl.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac5767fa451aef18983589a9fa98c3da8edea68b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/ac5767fa451aef18983589a9fa98c3da8edea68b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/4fd73f1960d9b88824ff6fad6ccc42e1a318d054","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/4fd73f1960d9b88824ff6fad6ccc42e1a318d054","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKDRmZDczZjE5NjBkOWI4ODgyNGZmNmZhZDZjY2M0MmUxYTMxOGQwNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/45eeb60772eb30110fef8bb21fa2329d5f3e322b","sha":"45eeb60772eb30110fef8bb21fa2329d5f3e322b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/45eeb60772eb30110fef8bb21fa2329d5f3e322b"}],"sha":"4fd73f1960d9b88824ff6fad6ccc42e1a318d054","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/4fd73f1960d9b88824ff6fad6ccc42e1a318d054"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/45eeb60772eb30110fef8bb21fa2329d5f3e322b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T13:51:23Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T13:51:23Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"docs: split SRS by domain, add ADR-0003 and PZEP-0002, verify DB design/ERDs for 5 services\n\n- Split docs/01-srs/podzone-srs.md''s functional requirements into one file\n  per requirement under auth/iam/onboarding/backoffice/partner folders;\n  podzone-srs.md now indexes them. Add SRS-IAM-003 (platform vs org admin\n  surface), SRS-IAM-004 (platform admin bootstrap gap), SRS-ONB-004 (store\n  request manual approval) — all marked planned/post-backbone per recovery\n  scope. Correct SRS-ONB-004''s initial claim that approve/reject RPCs don''t\n  exist (they do, per controller.go:44-45 and interactor.go:194-206) and\n  narrow the real gap to FE wiring + missing cross-tenant query.\n- Add ADR-0003 (Proposed): platform-scope roles currently grant no implicit\n  cross-tenant store access; document the gap and a candidate audited\n  override mechanism, found while debugging a 403 on onboarding''s resource\n  inventory screen.\n- Add PZEP-0002 (Draft): cmd/iam-bootstrap CLI design for granting the\n  first platform_owner and break-glass recovery, since no such path exists\n  in code today (AddPlatformRole requires an existing platform admin).\n- Verify DB design docs for auth/iam/backoffice/onboarding/partner against\n  real migrations/structs; iam was already complete (32/32 tables, earlier\n  \"missing 8\" claim was a header-matching false positive) — reorganize its\n  single giant ER diagram into an overview + 6 per-group diagrams matching\n  the Tables section. Same split applied to auth/backoffice/onboarding for\n  readability; onboarding verified with zero drift.\n- Wire the store-readiness contract into the frontend integration gap\n  tracked in backbone-flow-refactor.md and traceability-matrix.md; add the\n  corresponding agent task doc.\n- Reflow two paragraphs in document-standard.md to single lines (no content\n  change) and bump go.mod''s Go toolchain 1.26.0 -> 1.26.5, reorder its tool\n  list alphabetically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b8f06ad0d6498cf879c30a87396822dcc3b6baa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/b8f06ad0d6498cf879c30a87396822dcc3b6baa7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/45eeb60772eb30110fef8bb21fa2329d5f3e322b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/45eeb60772eb30110fef8bb21fa2329d5f3e322b","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKDQ1ZWViNjA3NzJlYjMwMTEwZmVmOGJiMjFmYTIzMjlkNWYzZTMyMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/08ce67f205e3ec5d9ae3c4cfccd1059142f7fdd1","sha":"08ce67f205e3ec5d9ae3c4cfccd1059142f7fdd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/08ce67f205e3ec5d9ae3c4cfccd1059142f7fdd1"}],"sha":"45eeb60772eb30110fef8bb21fa2329d5f3e322b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/45eeb60772eb30110fef8bb21fa2329d5f3e322b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/08ce67f205e3ec5d9ae3c4cfccd1059142f7fdd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T15:25:16Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T15:25:16Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"fix(frontend): scope MFE remote loading to the active docker-dev profile\n\nNarrow profiles (PROFILE=iam/backoffice/onboarding) white-screened on\n/admin — the default post-login landing page is owned by the onboarding\nremote regardless of which profile is active, but __MFE_ONBOARDING__ was\ncomputed from whether VITE_ONBOARDING_REMOTE_URL happened to be set, and\nservices.yml always provides a default value for all three remote URLs\nno matter the profile. So every profile tried to fetch remotes that were\nnever started (e.g. PROFILE=iam never starts onboarding-remote), instead\nof falling back to the page already bundled locally into the HOST for\nexactly this case (apps/onboarding/src/pages/AdminHomePage.tsx via the\n__MFE_ONBOARDING__ ? remote : local branch in routes.ts).\n\n- Makefile docker-dev: export PROFILE=$(PROFILE) into the docker compose\n  invocation so it''s visible as a shell env var, not just a Make variable.\n- services.yml frontend service: added VITE_ACTIVE_PROFILES: ${PROFILE:-full}.\n- vite.config.ts: __MFE_BACKOFFICE__/__MFE_IAM__/__MFE_ONBOARDING__ now\n  derive from VITE_ACTIVE_PROFILES (does this profile actually start that\n  remote?) instead of remote-URL-var presence. Falls back to \"full\" when\n  VITE_ACTIVE_PROFILES is unset, matching prior behavior for anyone\n  bypassing the Makefile with a raw `docker compose up`.\n\nAlso fixed docker-dev-down: it ran `docker compose down` with no\n--profile flag. Every service in services.yml is profiles-gated\n(backoffice/iam/onboarding/full — none default), and Compose does not\ntreat a profiled service as in-scope for `down` unless a matching\n--profile is passed, so containers started under any single-profile run\nwere never actually torn down by `make docker-dev-down` — confirmed\nlive: containers from a `PROFILE=backoffice` run 41 minutes into an\n`iam` session were still up. Every service already lists `full` in its\nprofiles array, so `--profile full` brings the whole set into scope.\nVerified: `docker compose --profile full ... config --services` now\nlists all 24 services (vs. only the profile-less infras.yml services\nbefore); ran `make docker-dev-down` live and confirmed zero podzone-*\ncontainers remain (`docker ps -a` empty).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a22be936077677353d59e7bd949489ea05d788c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/a22be936077677353d59e7bd949489ea05d788c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/08ce67f205e3ec5d9ae3c4cfccd1059142f7fdd1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/08ce67f205e3ec5d9ae3c4cfccd1059142f7fdd1","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKDA4Y2U2N2YyMDVlM2VjNWQ5YWUzYzRjZmNjZDEwNTkxNDJmN2ZkZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/37f4186c6babecd71953f4c5e192a10081ce0adf","sha":"37f4186c6babecd71953f4c5e192a10081ce0adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/37f4186c6babecd71953f4c5e192a10081ce0adf"}],"sha":"08ce67f205e3ec5d9ae3c4cfccd1059142f7fdd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/08ce67f205e3ec5d9ae3c4cfccd1059142f7fdd1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/37f4186c6babecd71953f4c5e192a10081ce0adf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T14:26:41Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T14:26:41Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"chore(docker): cap mem/cpu on all dev containers, bound kafka/connect JVM heap\n\nIdle stack was using ~3.5GB across 22 containers with no per-container\nceiling. Kafka in particular had no KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS set, showing periodic\nCPU spikes to 90%+ (JVM GC on an unbounded default heap) and ~800MB\nresident. cdc-connect (Debezium, also JVM) had the same gap.\n\n- KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS: -Xms256m -Xmx512m (kafka), -Xms128m -Xmx384m\n  (cdc-connect) — neither had a heap bound before.\n- mem_limit/cpus added to every service in both compose files:\n  - x-go-dev-common anchor (512m/1cpu) covers all 10 Go services\n    (auth/iam/onboarding/backoffice/partner/catalog/grpc-gateway,\n    2 workers, dev-bootstrap) in one place.\n  - MFE remotes (backoffice/iam/onboarding-remote, vite build --watch +\n    preview) get 1024m/1.5cpu — these run 3 separate Node/esbuild\n    processes each holding file-watcher state for the whole bind-mounted\n    frontend/ tree, the biggest FE-side consumer at ~400-500MB baseline\n    each.\n  - HOST frontend (vite dev): 768m/1.5cpu.\n  - Infra tier: postgres/mongo 512m/1cpu, kafka/elasticsearch 768m/1-1.5cpu,\n    cdc-connect 512m/1cpu, apisix 384m/1cpu, kibana 512m/1cpu,\n    pgbouncer/redis/etcd/apisix-dashboard/apisix-init 64-256m/0.25-0.5cpu.\n\nValidated via `docker compose --profile full config` — anchor merge\nresolves correctly (536870912 bytes = 512m etc.), no YAML conflicts.\nNot yet verified that any service actually needs more than its cap under\nload (e.g. a cold `go build` or a large frontend rebuild) — if a\ncontainer gets OOM-killed or CPU-throttled during real work, raise that\nspecific service''s limit rather than removing limits stack-wide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f853f45081f0f2c6f99db717dd9d143c9f879257","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/f853f45081f0f2c6f99db717dd9d143c9f879257"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/37f4186c6babecd71953f4c5e192a10081ce0adf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/37f4186c6babecd71953f4c5e192a10081ce0adf","node_id":"C_kwDOMdFIKNoAKDM3ZjQxODZjNmJhYmVjZDcxOTUzZjRjNWUxOTJhMTAwODFjZTBhZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99/podzone/commit/82a14dfe2b09f45d03ed63e293abd0f06a0b0a2c","sha":"82a14dfe2b09f45d03ed63e293abd0f06a0b0a2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/82a14dfe2b09f45d03ed63e293abd0f06a0b0a2c"}],"sha":"37f4186c6babecd71953f4c5e192a10081ce0adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/37f4186c6babecd71953f4c5e192a10081ce0adf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuannm99","id":81021902,"login":"tuannm99","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDIxOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/commits/82a14dfe2b09f45d03ed63e293abd0f06a0b0a2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T13:52:30Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T13:52:30Z","email":"gm.tuannm99@gmail.com","name":"tuannm99"},"message":"docs: move sequence diagrams into per-service api-design.md, add C3/C4 + API contract\n\nA sequence diagram is only useful next to the usecase/API it describes —\ndocs/02-architecture-overall/05-sequences.md was a flat cross-cutting file\nmixing auth/iam/onboarding/backoffice flows with no connection to the API\ncontracts they implement. Deleted it and redistributed its 9 diagrams into\neach owning service''s new api-design.md, alongside a C3 component view and\nthe full gRPC/HTTP/GraphQL API surface — completing the per-service detail\ndesign started in the ERD pass (README.md + db-design.md already existed).\n\nNew files (one per service with real code — auth/iam/onboarding/backoffice/\npartner; catalog/storefront/gateway stay stub-only per legacy-inventory.md):\ndocs/03-architecture-detail-design/services/<name>/api-design.md, each with\nC3: Component View, full API surface table, C4: Sequences Per Usecase, and\nCross-Service Dependencies.\n\nDiagrams were reproduced from the old file as a starting point and verified\nagainst current code, not regenerated blind — several had drifted and were\ncorrected with the drift noted inline rather than silently fixed:\n\n- Both onboarding diagrams mislabeled the KV route projection as \"Mongo\n  runtime_kv\" — it''s Redis/Valkey (already corrected elsewhere in\n  data-ownership.md and onboarding/db-design.md). Fixed here too.\n- \"Store Onboarding Request to Ready\" showed a generic worker round-trip;\n  real code splits it into ProcessNextStoreRequest (claim+plan) and\n  FinalizeNextStoreRequest (persist+publish+mark-ready) as two distinct\n  interactor calls. Corrected, drift noted.\n- \"Create Routed Order Recommendation\" showed a single-table write; real\n  code dual-writes into both routed_orders and customer_orders in the same\n  call. Corrected, drift noted.\n- Partner''s tenant-authorization sequence was duplicated between README.md\n  and the new api-design.md — moved into api-design.md only, README.md now\n  has a one-line pointer.\n\nNew findings surfaced and noted inline (not fixed — out of scope for a docs\npass): onboarding''s `Controller.UpdateStoreRequestStatus` HTTP handler has\nzero route registrations anywhere in the repo (dead code); IAM''s real gRPC\nsurface is 78 RPCs across the CQRS split (command+query), well above the\n\"~60\" estimate from the earlier ERD pass.\n\nAlso fixed:\n- docs/03-architecture-detail-design/services/README.md''s IAM table count\n  was wrong (32, carried over from the original ERD fork''s report) — the\n  actual db-design.md documents 24 distinct tables. Corrected to the\n  number that''s actually verifiable in the file.\n- docs/02-architecture-overall/01-c4.md''s C3/C4 sections still referenced\n  bare pre-renumbering filenames (modules.md, sequences.md, code-map.md,\n  transport-contracts.md, async-messaging.md, system-context.md,\n  containers.md) that were missed by the earlier renumbering pass''s sed\n  script (it only matched fully-prefixed paths, not bare filenames used\n  without a directory). Fixed all of them and repointed the C3/C4 sections\n  at the new per-service docs.\n- 02-architecture-overall/README.md: removed sequences.md from scope/reading\n  order, added an explicit note that C3/C4 now live per-service.\n- traceability-matrix.md: redirected the two SRS-ONB references that\n  pointed at 05-sequences.md, and upgraded two Contract/DB cells (SRS-IAM-001,\n  SRS-ONB-001) from TBD to real links now that the underlying contracts are\n  documented in the new api-design.md files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d269068c7735ecd48324ba5e8cc267fef8c54740","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/trees/d269068c7735ecd48324ba5e8cc267fef8c54740"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuannm99/podzone/git/commits/82a14dfe2b09f45d03ed63e293abd0f06a0b0a2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81021902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuannm99/foll